1
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:19,079
Halime!

2
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:21,839
-Halime!
-Where are you?

3
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:23,479
My daughter!

4
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:27,999
Halime!

5
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:32,119
Alps, get in the water!

6
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:33,879
Check everywhere!

7
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:37,399
Halime!

8
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:39,079
Soldiers!

9
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:42,439
Halime!

10
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:46,719
Check under the water too!

11
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:48,239
Soldiers!

12
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:50,919
Do not come back without finding Poena!

13
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,679
She is still calling her Poena!

14
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:54,319
What did you do to my daughter, huh?!

15
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:57,359
What did you do to my daughter
that made her try to take her own life?

16
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:59,639
It's all because of you!

17
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:02,559
If you had not wanted
her, she would still be alive!

18
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:04,119
You killed her!

19
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:04,799
Bala.

20
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:07,359
I will kill you!
I will kill you!

21
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:09,319
Sofia. Pull yourself together!

22
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:10,839
Pull yourself together!

23
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:12,279
We are looking for Halime!

24
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:14,319
We are looking for Halime, Bala!

25
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:18,679
Go to the left!

26
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:21,439
You will go and look for
her with your soldiers! Go!

27
00:03:27,760 --> 00:03:29,439
Soldiers!

28
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:35,159
Bala.

29
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:38,559
We are looking for Halime, come on!

30
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:43,479
Halime!

31
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:19,039
Claudius and his dogs...

32
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:21,639
They are covering their tracks but...

33
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:24,959
...those fools do not know that
we will never go back before...

34
00:04:24,960 --> 00:04:28,919
...we take the revenge of our innocent people.

35
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:34,119
Oghuz senses and sees every
kind of treacherous trick for sure.

36
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:36,839
We will make them learn this, Hasan brother.

37
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:39,239
For sure.

38
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:05,319
Commander Claudius. -Tell me.

39
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:07,239
Osman's Beys Koca and Hasan...

40
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:09,519
...are following us with their Alps, sir.

41
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:10,309
Good

42
00:05:10,309 --> 00:05:13,679
I was waiting for them to separate
from the herd, so they would follow us.

43
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:16,199
-How many are there?
-Not many, sir.

44
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:17,559
Don't stop them.

45
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:18,599
Let them follow us.

46
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:22,279
Understood.

47
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:34,719
Halime!

48
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:36,519
My daughter!

49
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:38,159
Poena!

50
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:40,519
Poena, where are you?

51
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:42,679
Halime!

52
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:46,799
Halime!

53
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:50,159
My daughter, where are you?

54
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:52,919
-Halime!
-Poena!

55
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:56,039
My Allah, protect her... Halime!

56
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:58,079
Where are you my daughter?

57
00:06:58,760 --> 00:07:01,199
My daughter!

58
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:05,079
Halime!

59
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:10,319
Halime!

60
00:07:11,640 --> 00:07:13,279
My daughter!

61
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:17,719
Halime... Where are you sister?

62
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:19,639
Where?

63
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:21,879
Halime!

64
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:27,159
There are tracks here!

65
00:07:29,960 --> 00:07:31,439
My Bey!

66
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:33,639
My Bey! There are tracks here!

67
00:07:43,440 --> 00:07:45,719
The tracks are coming from this side.

68
00:07:45,720 --> 00:07:47,279
It goes there.

69
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:49,079
And after that point...

70
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:52,439
Poena is alive!

71
00:07:56,760 --> 00:07:58,919
Osman, Halime is running away from us.

72
00:07:58,920 --> 00:08:01,559
What if she is not alright? What if
something bad happened to her?

73
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:04,559
Don't worry. We will split into three groups.

74
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:08,559
Bala, you will go to the
southern side with Sofia.

75
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:11,679
Orhan, you will climb to
the hill on the northern side.

76
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:12,799
What about you?

77
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:14,839
We will go this way with the Alps.

78
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:16,319
May our war be blessed.

79
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:17,559
Come on Sisters! Come on!

80
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:19,199
Come on Alps!

81
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:39,119
This is a gift from your warriors, Orlok Kucar.

82
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:12,799
Apart from this woman, huh?

83
00:11:16,760 --> 00:11:18,919
She's the shahzade's wife.

84
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:30,239
A son and daughter of Osman's is enough for me.

85
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:34,519
This woman is useless for me.

86
00:11:35,520 --> 00:11:37,239
Kill her.

87
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:04,319
Don't.

88
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:10,279
You care about your wife, huh?

89
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:11,999
Bey's son

90
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:18,239
Obviously, she will be useful.

91
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:19,679
Don't kill her.

92
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:27,239
If you harm me or my wife

93
00:12:27,920 --> 00:12:33,239
...you should know that your fate will
be more terrible than your messengers.

94
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:38,359
Mind your own fate, Bey's son.

95
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:50,999
-Osman's daughter?
-Your warriors are after her.

96
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:54,799
Soon, she will appear before you too.

97
00:12:55,040 --> 00:12:58,119
-Fatma...
-Not Fatma. Halime!

98
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:02,679
The woman called Sofia fooled everyone.

99
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:06,759
The girl they call Meryem is actually Halime.

100
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:18,399
Is Meryem my sister?

101
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:20,519
How come?

102
00:13:22,800 --> 00:13:25,919
Put them inside the cage!

103
00:13:26,120 --> 00:13:28,759
-Get off!
Meryem...

104
00:13:28,920 --> 00:13:30,279
Get off!

105
00:13:31,880 --> 00:13:34,759
How come? How come?

106
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:40,879
My noble servant Claudius
will end this alliance!

107
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:55,079
You exposed your greatest plan to
have an alliance with Osman, huh, Sofia?

108
00:13:58,080 --> 00:14:05,599
Halime is going to pass away
before she meets her family.

109
00:14:06,520 --> 00:14:10,959
And the alliance will end.

110
00:14:11,920 --> 00:14:14,159
How is that possible?

111
00:14:14,760 --> 00:14:19,639
Vile dogs.

112
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:23,519
-Gonca, are you alright?
-Yes. You?

113
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:24,719
I'm fine.

114
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:38,479
Poena, stop!

115
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:42,479
They're after me, coming.

116
00:14:46,800 --> 00:14:48,399
Who are they?

117
00:15:08,080 --> 00:15:11,079
Halime! Halime!

118
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:15,399
Alps, you go this way.

119
00:15:21,800 --> 00:15:22,879
Halime!

120
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:27,879
-Father...
-Halime!

121
00:15:32,920 --> 00:15:34,319
Osman Bey.

122
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:37,119
My daughter.

123
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:39,399
I've found you.

124
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:43,159
I've found you. Give me your hand.

125
00:15:44,680 --> 00:15:47,039
Come on, come here.

126
00:15:49,040 --> 00:15:51,479
Come on, girl. Everybody is waiting for you.

127
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:55,759
I can't look at you in the
eyes after what happened.

128
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:00,719
I carry your blood, but...

129
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:05,199
...my soul is a sinner.

130
00:16:05,560 --> 00:16:08,519
What do you mean? Not at all.

131
00:16:08,960 --> 00:16:10,639
It's not your fault.

132
00:16:11,600 --> 00:16:14,999
Come on, my dear. I'm your father.

133
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,079
Come to me.

134
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:20,839
As long as I live, I will
always have this disgrace.

135
00:16:23,280 --> 00:16:26,799
-I can't.
-No, my little gazelle.

136
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:29,079
You won't.

137
00:16:30,120 --> 00:16:32,199
Let's get over this together.

138
00:16:32,480 --> 00:16:34,039
Come.

139
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:37,839
Everybody is waiting for you.

140
00:16:43,760 --> 00:16:45,559
Come finish our longing.

141
00:16:48,760 --> 00:16:50,239
Halime!

142
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:56,479
Halime!

143
00:16:58,360 --> 00:17:02,639
Whoever stands against my
daughter, I will storm against them.

144
00:17:07,200 --> 00:17:10,439
You and I will fight bravely now.

145
00:18:26,800 --> 00:18:28,159
Father...

146
00:18:38,160 --> 00:18:39,759
I'm here, my Bey!

147
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:43,359
Orhan.

148
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:48,839
-Without swords, huh, my Bey?
-Without swords.

149
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:23,959
What makes those dogs
strong is their looks, my Bey.

150
00:19:23,960 --> 00:19:27,679
They wait for the enemy's
move first and then they attack.

151
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:30,079
Still, we will hit.

152
00:19:30,400 --> 00:19:32,599
We will beat them.

153
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:37,639
My Bey!

154
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:40,159
We're here, my Bey!

155
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:44,439
The enemy's tricks are shattered
on the faithful chests of the warriors.

156
00:19:44,640 --> 00:19:45,839
Ya Allah!

157
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:49,959
Alps, shoot arrows!

158
00:20:01,920 --> 00:20:03,279
Cerkutay.

159
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:06,919
Are these who you mentioned?

160
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:08,719
Yes, my Bey.

161
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:11,519
Orlok Kucar's warriors.

162
00:20:13,360 --> 00:20:15,759
What is Kucar up to, my Bey?

163
00:20:15,760 --> 00:20:17,239
-Why did he attack you?

164
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:20,519
Not me. They're after Halime for revenge.

165
00:20:20,520 --> 00:20:23,039
Vipers are doing what suit them again, my Bey.

166
00:20:23,240 --> 00:20:25,679
With Allah's help, they won't succeed.

167
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:27,279
For sure.

168
00:20:27,520 --> 00:20:29,319
As Kucar knows everything,

169
00:20:29,320 --> 00:20:33,239
...he won't stop until he
gets what he wants, my Bey.

170
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:35,959
Don't worry. We'll find Halime first.

171
00:20:36,320 --> 00:20:39,319
I will destroy who is trying to harm her.

172
00:20:39,480 --> 00:20:41,959
This way. Come on.

173
00:20:49,080 --> 00:20:50,519
Halime!

174
00:20:51,080 --> 00:20:52,159
Poena!

175
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:54,479
Halime, where are you?

176
00:20:55,640 --> 00:20:56,679
Poena!

177
00:20:57,680 --> 00:20:58,959
Halime!

178
00:21:08,080 --> 00:21:09,359
Halime..

179
00:21:14,840 --> 00:21:16,319
Halime!

180
00:21:17,520 --> 00:21:19,559
Bala Hatun! Bala Hatun!

181
00:21:26,320 --> 00:21:27,999
Halime..

182
00:21:47,560 --> 00:21:50,439
Don't do this to me, my girl.

183
00:21:50,840 --> 00:21:52,919
Halime! Halime!

184
00:21:53,240 --> 00:21:55,119
“My dear! My baby!
-Poena!

185
00:21:55,400 --> 00:21:56,999
Halime! Halime!

186
00:22:00,080 --> 00:22:01,719
-Halime!
-Bala.

187
00:22:02,520 --> 00:22:03,919
Halime!

188
00:22:05,760 --> 00:22:07,799
Halime! Halime!

189
00:22:08,840 --> 00:22:10,199
Hold her.

190
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:13,959
Get her up. Halime. My baby.

191
00:22:14,400 --> 00:22:18,159
Halime, my dear... Open your eyes.

192
00:22:18,440 --> 00:22:21,079
Bala. Bala.

193
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:24,119
Is she alive?

194
00:22:27,400 --> 00:22:29,559
She isn't breathing.

195
00:22:32,920 --> 00:22:34,319
Halime.

196
00:22:35,200 --> 00:22:36,999
Halime. Halime, my dear.

197
00:22:37,120 --> 00:22:39,799
My dear, wake up. Wake up, Halime.

198
00:22:39,880 --> 00:22:41,239
Wake up, my dear.

199
00:22:41,760 --> 00:22:44,879
-Bala...
Don't! Open your eyes, my dear.

200
00:22:45,440 --> 00:22:49,599
Wake up, my baby.
Halime, come on. Come on.

201
00:22:49,760 --> 00:22:52,719
Don't do this. Open your eyes, Halime.

202
00:22:52,880 --> 00:22:55,559
Open your eyes, my dear. Halime!
-Poena...

203
00:22:55,800 --> 00:22:57,759
-No, no. -Bala?

204
00:22:58,120 --> 00:23:00,319
-Osman, she isn't waking up.
-Halime!

205
00:23:00,480 --> 00:23:02,919
She isn't waking up. Halime?

206
00:23:03,120 --> 00:23:04,999
-Halime, open your eyes.
-Halime.

207
00:23:05,160 --> 00:23:06,919
She isn't waking up, Osman.

208
00:23:07,200 --> 00:23:09,679
-My sister...
She isn't waking up, Osman.

209
00:23:09,760 --> 00:23:11,119
-Halime.
-Halime.

210
00:23:11,560 --> 00:23:13,759
Water. Water.

211
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:15,799
Bring water!

212
00:23:15,920 --> 00:23:17,479
-Alps.
-Bring water.

213
00:23:17,640 --> 00:23:19,959
-My Bey, water.
-She has a wound.

214
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:24,999
-Open your eyes, my dear.
-Come on, baby.

215
00:23:25,400 --> 00:23:26,599
Halime... Halime.

216
00:23:33,440 --> 00:23:35,279
-She's waken up.
-She is alive.

217
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:36,559
She's alive.

218
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:39,399
She's waken

219
00:23:44,080 --> 00:23:45,399
-Aunt.
She's alive.

220
00:23:45,600 --> 00:23:47,359
My little bird...

221
00:23:48,080 --> 00:23:50,319
-My dear.
-Bala Hatun.

222
00:23:53,080 --> 00:23:56,439
-Come on.
-Thanks to Allah. Thanks to Allah.

223
00:23:57,680 --> 00:23:59,079
Osman Bey.

224
00:23:59,080 --> 00:24:01,159
My Halime.

225
00:24:01,400 --> 00:24:03,039
Come, my daughter, come.

226
00:24:03,040 --> 00:24:05,119
Come, take a breath, come.

227
00:24:10,800 --> 00:24:13,599
Are you alright, my daughter? You are injured.

228
00:24:13,600 --> 00:24:16,759
Every time you call me your daughter...

229
00:24:17,400 --> 00:24:19,719
..it hurts me even more.

230
00:24:23,520 --> 00:24:25,839
My wound is bleeding more, my Bey.

231
00:24:26,240 --> 00:24:31,239
You will always be ashamed
of having a daughter like me.

232
00:24:33,880 --> 00:24:36,199
Is that even possible?

233
00:24:36,480 --> 00:24:39,079
You are our blood, our child.

234
00:24:39,080 --> 00:24:42,199
Don't say such words, don't, my child.

235
00:24:44,200 --> 00:24:47,919
Sister, come. Let's warm you up.

236
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:50,399
Alps, come and help. Bring the horses, hurry.

237
00:24:50,400 --> 00:24:52,039
Come on, my child, come on, slowly.

238
00:24:52,040 --> 00:24:53,959
In the name of Allah.

239
00:24:54,840 --> 00:24:56,399
Come on, my daughter.

240
00:24:57,200 --> 00:24:59,799
Come on, my daughter, come on.

241
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:06,319
I told you this wouldn't be easy.

242
00:25:06,320 --> 00:25:08,279
Shut up Sofia!

243
00:25:10,480 --> 00:25:13,879
Osman, who were those behind Halime?

244
00:25:15,680 --> 00:25:17,279
Kucar.

245
00:25:18,320 --> 00:25:20,159
Kucar found out about Halime.

246
00:25:20,160 --> 00:25:21,799
Kucar?

247
00:25:22,080 --> 00:25:25,879
He wants to prevent our alliance, huh?

248
00:25:25,880 --> 00:25:27,199
So?

249
00:25:27,200 --> 00:25:29,399
Do you believe me now?

250
00:25:35,800 --> 00:25:38,159
What if they learned about Alaeddin?

251
00:25:54,520 --> 00:25:56,959
Which way did he go, Hasan brother?

252
00:25:56,960 --> 00:26:00,999
Tell me, tell me so we can find
him and cut off the head of the snake.

253
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:04,319
The tracks spread in all
directions from here, Koca Bey.

254
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:18,479
Hasan brother!

255
00:26:20,480 --> 00:26:22,999
You dastard..

256
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:26,519
So, you realized we were following you.

257
00:26:27,080 --> 00:26:28,999
You are right, old man.

258
00:26:30,320 --> 00:26:34,159
Osman's wanderer hunters now you are my prey!

259
00:26:34,160 --> 00:26:36,919
You will know who is the
hunter and who is the prey...

260
00:26:36,920 --> 00:26:40,919
...when your head is on a stake, dog.

261
00:26:43,360 --> 00:26:46,039
Hold on, Hasan brother, are you alright?

262
00:26:46,040 --> 00:26:47,839
I'm alright, Koca Bey.

263
00:26:51,640 --> 00:26:56,839
This wound won't make me fall until
I take this dastard's life, Koca Bey.

264
00:26:57,480 --> 00:27:03,079
When the battle starts, go without being
noticed and inform Osman Bey, my valiant.

265
00:27:04,960 --> 00:27:07,679
Soldiers, attack!

266
00:27:54,280 --> 00:27:55,879
Dastard!

267
00:27:55,880 --> 00:27:58,599
You can't with this wound, Hasan Bey.

268
00:27:58,600 --> 00:28:01,959
Let's retreat to Tavsantepe
lose our tracks there...

269
00:28:02,080 --> 00:28:04,279
...and wait for Osman Bey. Let's go!

270
00:28:04,280 --> 00:28:08,839
Alps, retreat, come on!

271
00:28:19,520 --> 00:28:24,119
This will show Osman Bey the
direction we are going, come on.

272
00:28:31,600 --> 00:28:37,199
You wanderers, with the messenger
you sent, you will trap Osman.

273
00:28:41,400 --> 00:28:42,879
No.

274
00:28:43,800 --> 00:28:45,919
I don't understand, Alaeddin.

275
00:28:46,600 --> 00:28:48,719
If Meryem is Halime...

276
00:28:48,880 --> 00:28:50,239
...Sofia would have...

277
00:28:50,240 --> 00:28:54,319
She turned her into our
enemy and sent her to us, Hatun.

278
00:28:56,680 --> 00:28:59,639
She turned my sister
into a sword for her hatred.

279
00:28:59,760 --> 00:29:02,079
Devil...

280
00:29:02,080 --> 00:29:06,359
My Allah... My Allah, what
kind of evilness is this?

281
00:29:06,880 --> 00:29:10,519
May You protect her from the
evil of these demons, my Allah.

282
00:29:11,080 --> 00:29:14,079
My wrath has become a mountain.

283
00:29:14,200 --> 00:29:18,079
My wrath has become an
avalanche, son of the Bey.

284
00:29:20,720 --> 00:29:23,599
It's pouring down on you.

285
00:29:24,160 --> 00:29:25,759
Look.

286
00:29:26,640 --> 00:29:28,999
Let my sister go.

287
00:29:30,280 --> 00:29:32,039
Let my Hatun go.

288
00:29:32,040 --> 00:29:33,159
Alaeddin..

289
00:29:33,160 --> 00:29:37,039
Osman Bey's son, the Shahzade is here.

290
00:29:37,120 --> 00:29:39,679
What more do you need?

291
00:29:42,640 --> 00:29:48,199
Your sister and your Hatun
will share the same fate as you.

292
00:29:48,280 --> 00:29:53,039
They will stand before my great Khan Olcaytu.

293
00:29:53,080 --> 00:29:57,959
If your Hatun is pregnant...

294
00:29:59,120 --> 00:30:02,559
...your Shahzade will face the same fate.

295
00:30:03,080 --> 00:30:07,599
That baby will share the same fate as you.

296
00:30:14,240 --> 00:30:17,239
You were reading El-Medinetu'l-Fazila.

297
00:30:20,880 --> 00:30:22,679
I saw you.

298
00:30:24,160 --> 00:30:25,959
Tell me.

299
00:30:26,560 --> 00:30:29,439
Don't you ever understand what you read?

300
00:30:29,760 --> 00:30:35,759
Don't you ever take a lesson from the
command of our glorious Prophet?

301
00:30:36,440 --> 00:30:37,839
He said..

302
00:30:38,760 --> 00:30:41,799
"In war, do not touch women, children...

303
00:30:41,800 --> 00:30:47,079
...or the elderly, even if
they are your enemies."

304
00:30:49,520 --> 00:30:53,359
You know this, you know this for sure.

305
00:30:59,040 --> 00:31:04,879
So you are not just a shepherd, son of the Bey?

306
00:31:05,040 --> 00:31:08,319
You also have some knowledge, is that true?

307
00:31:09,400 --> 00:31:11,999
Right. Right.

308
00:31:13,680 --> 00:31:16,799
While at war against oppression and infidelity.

309
00:31:17,120 --> 00:31:22,559
Do you think the scholar's knowledge
falls behind the Bey's bravery?

310
00:31:22,560 --> 00:31:25,719
Esenbike was also a woman.

311
00:31:25,800 --> 00:31:29,159
So, you didn't kill her, huh?

312
00:31:31,640 --> 00:31:34,279
She killed many innocent people.

313
00:31:35,040 --> 00:31:40,799
If we had her in our hands,
her blood would be halal for us.

314
00:31:41,880 --> 00:31:44,079
But know this.

315
00:31:44,880 --> 00:31:49,279
We did not kill her, Sofia did.

316
00:31:50,040 --> 00:31:51,599
Sofia.

317
00:32:02,520 --> 00:32:05,839
While not in such a battle...

318
00:32:06,640 --> 00:32:08,719
...Sofia would never do this since...

319
00:32:08,800 --> 00:32:14,159
...she would never want to
face my glorious Khan Olcaytu.

320
00:32:16,120 --> 00:32:18,439
She wouldn't do such a thing.

321
00:32:21,960 --> 00:32:24,119
You will see.

322
00:32:24,880 --> 00:32:26,799
You will see.

323
00:32:27,400 --> 00:32:29,439
You all will see.

324
00:32:47,520 --> 00:32:49,079
Meryem.

325
00:32:51,240 --> 00:32:53,359
What happened to them?

326
00:32:57,880 --> 00:33:01,319
-Welcome, my Bey.
-Welcome, Osman Bey. -Welcome, Osman Bey.

327
00:33:01,320 --> 00:33:04,119
You still haven't said anything, Osman.

328
00:33:05,000 --> 00:33:09,199
As you ordered, we placed the Alps
and strengthened the Derince outpost.

329
00:33:09,200 --> 00:33:11,199
Keep protecting that place.

330
00:33:11,200 --> 00:33:13,439
You still haven't said anything.

331
00:33:17,760 --> 00:33:19,999
We will talk in the tent.

332
00:33:34,120 --> 00:33:37,999
What happened to you? Where have you been?

333
00:33:39,640 --> 00:33:44,479
Mother, what is this Sofia snake doing here?

334
00:33:45,760 --> 00:33:47,599
Tell me.

335
00:33:47,640 --> 00:33:49,079
Kismet.

336
00:33:49,080 --> 00:33:51,759
Prepare my Alaeddin's tent.

337
00:33:52,560 --> 00:33:53,919
What?

338
00:33:53,960 --> 00:33:56,199
My Halime will stay there.

339
00:33:56,200 --> 00:33:57,719
My sister...

340
00:33:58,760 --> 00:34:03,359
Mother, have you found my sister?
Where is she? Tell me, brother.

341
00:34:03,360 --> 00:34:04,719
Mother.

342
00:34:05,360 --> 00:34:09,039
I will tell you, daughter. I will tell you.

343
00:34:09,600 --> 00:34:11,438
Halime is here.

344
00:34:12,400 --> 00:34:14,879
Your sister is standing right in front of you.

345
00:34:18,360 --> 00:34:21,799
She is not Meryem. She is Halime.

346
00:34:25,600 --> 00:34:27,039
What?

347
00:34:29,400 --> 00:34:31,359
Mother, what are you saying?

348
00:34:31,360 --> 00:34:34,679
I will explain. But right
now, your sister is very tired.

349
00:34:34,679 --> 00:34:36,958
Let her rest for a bit, alright, my daughter?

350
00:34:38,120 --> 00:34:41,279
Come on. Come on, my daughter.

351
00:34:56,000 --> 00:34:59,159
Orhan. What's happening?

352
00:35:00,400 --> 00:35:01,959
Sofia.

353
00:35:02,520 --> 00:35:07,039
That snake Sofia planned
a game. She did all this.

354
00:35:08,920 --> 00:35:13,559
She betrayed us, huh?
She betrayed her own blood.

355
00:35:14,920 --> 00:35:17,519
She became Sofia's puppet.

356
00:35:21,560 --> 00:35:24,399
Sister. My Fatma.

357
00:35:24,800 --> 00:35:25,959
My sister...

358
00:35:26,080 --> 00:35:28,359
Why are you saying that?

359
00:35:28,360 --> 00:35:32,479
She is our sister.
She is our sibling.

360
00:35:32,480 --> 00:35:36,559
No. My sister is in the grave.

361
00:35:37,280 --> 00:35:40,359
She died the day my
mother found her in that river.

362
00:36:09,560 --> 00:36:12,119
Everyone looks at me with doubt

363
00:36:13,120 --> 00:36:15,599
They know I deceived them.

364
00:36:17,000 --> 00:36:21,119
They don't know you, and you don't know them.

365
00:36:21,320 --> 00:36:23,959
But we will forget about the past.

366
00:36:23,960 --> 00:36:25,999
We will start again.

367
00:36:27,680 --> 00:36:31,639
I have no past to forget or remember.

368
00:36:34,160 --> 00:36:37,399
Poena is lost, Meryem is dead.

369
00:36:38,240 --> 00:36:41,919
Halime... Halime knows nothing.

370
00:36:41,920 --> 00:36:43,919
Look at me.

371
00:36:45,120 --> 00:36:50,639
I am your mother, and you
are my beautiful daughter.

372
00:36:51,720 --> 00:36:53,999
For now, knowing this is enough, alright?

373
00:36:54,720 --> 00:36:58,599
Now go to the tent, I'll bring you a dress.

374
00:36:59,000 --> 00:37:00,159
Come on, my daughter.

375
00:37:43,800 --> 00:37:46,759
Mongols or others...

376
00:37:48,240 --> 00:37:51,279
Whoever comes to these borders...

377
00:37:52,040 --> 00:37:55,242
...the Byzantine soldiers,
according to this peace

378
00:37:55,254 --> 00:37:58,279
agreement, will be under
my command, in my army.

379
00:38:10,360 --> 00:38:13,319
If Bursa is attacked...

380
00:38:18,480 --> 00:38:21,399
...then your Alps...

381
00:38:29,360 --> 00:38:31,879
...will be under my command.

382
00:38:45,120 --> 00:38:47,079
Then we agreed.

383
00:38:55,480 --> 00:38:58,879
From now on, we are friends, Osman Bey.

384
00:38:58,880 --> 00:39:01,399
Since we agreed on peace, I want Claudius.

385
00:39:08,520 --> 00:39:10,679
Claudius is a good commander, Osman Bey.

386
00:39:10,680 --> 00:39:15,639
As the Emperor said, I can
make him pledge allegiance you.

387
00:39:15,640 --> 00:39:18,879
No. The blood of my martyrs is on his hands.

388
00:39:18,880 --> 00:39:20,839
I will never let him join my army.

389
00:39:22,840 --> 00:39:28,239
Dead or alive, I will punish
him with my own hands.

390
00:39:28,640 --> 00:39:33,439
Now, as a symbol of this peace...

391
00:39:35,320 --> 00:39:38,039
...you will give me his head.

392
00:39:40,040 --> 00:39:44,399
If you try to oppose this...
-No, that won't happen.

393
00:39:46,440 --> 00:39:51,839
Claudius, with what he did, betrayed
not only me but the Emperor as well.

394
00:39:54,680 --> 00:39:58,239
Killing him won't break our peace.

395
00:40:18,440 --> 00:40:19,959
It's like a dream.

396
00:40:22,800 --> 00:40:24,599
If I had never left here

397
00:40:25,720 --> 00:40:27,879
...what would my life be like?

398
00:40:57,480 --> 00:40:59,159
You are angry with me, aren't you?

399
00:41:01,640 --> 00:41:03,199
Am I angry?

400
00:41:05,480 --> 00:41:10,559
If you weren't family

401
00:41:11,200 --> 00:41:14,079
...I would kill you without hesitation.

402
00:41:17,400 --> 00:41:21,799
You used me to enter the tribe.

403
00:41:22,040 --> 00:41:24,079
To spy on us.

404
00:41:25,520 --> 00:41:28,119
We shared our bread with you.

405
00:41:28,680 --> 00:41:30,879
We let you join our family.

406
00:41:31,480 --> 00:41:33,639
You betrayed us.

407
00:41:36,120 --> 00:41:39,519
What I did cannot be forgiven. I know that.

408
00:41:40,640 --> 00:41:42,119
I don't understand.

409
00:41:42,360 --> 00:41:44,719
How could a person do this to another one?

410
00:41:47,560 --> 00:41:49,439
I thought you were my enemy.

411
00:41:49,720 --> 00:41:53,879
You kept disappearing to send messages, right?

412
00:41:54,600 --> 00:41:57,279
It was you who told them
where the hidden tribe was.

413
00:41:58,360 --> 00:42:02,519
-You exposed our secrets one by one.
-Yes, I did.

414
00:42:03,960 --> 00:42:05,279
I did.

415
00:42:05,600 --> 00:42:09,519
I did everything to kill
Osman Bey and Bala Hatun.

416
00:42:10,800 --> 00:42:16,159
You also knew that my mother
didn't get burned in that cabin.

417
00:42:16,760 --> 00:42:22,479
And you let us lament and mourn.

418
00:42:23,200 --> 00:42:26,959
I thought my sorrow would
be gone while I watched yours.

419
00:42:28,520 --> 00:42:30,719
But it hurt me more.

420
00:42:31,640 --> 00:42:33,759
I thought you were my enemy.

421
00:42:34,120 --> 00:42:39,279
No, no. We wouldn't do this to even our enemy.

422
00:42:39,960 --> 00:42:43,159
You became Sofia's daughter.

423
00:42:43,280 --> 00:42:45,799
-You...
Fatma, this is enough.

424
00:42:46,160 --> 00:42:49,519
Mother, we can't trust this girl.

425
00:42:51,080 --> 00:42:53,759
She's not an ordinary girl but your sister.

426
00:42:55,600 --> 00:42:59,679
This girl is not my sister.

427
00:43:02,360 --> 00:43:03,999
-Fatma.
-Mother, leave me.

428
00:43:04,240 --> 00:43:06,879
-Don't do this, my dear.
-Mother, leave me.

429
00:43:13,400 --> 00:43:15,039
Halime.

430
00:43:16,000 --> 00:43:18,159
If you had let me die,

431
00:43:19,400 --> 00:43:21,319
...everything would be easier.

432
00:43:50,720 --> 00:43:54,199
We need to cauterize your wound, brother Hasan.

433
00:43:54,680 --> 00:43:58,319
But we can't make a fire now.

434
00:43:59,880 --> 00:44:01,439
Old man!

435
00:44:03,280 --> 00:44:04,999
You will be burned.

436
00:44:06,800 --> 00:44:09,559
Another fire will burn you, though.

437
00:44:10,160 --> 00:44:12,239
Which fire is that?

438
00:44:12,400 --> 00:44:14,239
My wrath's fire?

439
00:44:20,760 --> 00:44:23,799
You Turks have a saying... What was that?

440
00:44:24,680 --> 00:44:27,759
I'm a hero but it has no use?

441
00:44:31,240 --> 00:44:34,119
Something like that. Attack.

442
00:45:14,120 --> 00:45:18,359
...I will cut you into pieces and
make a thousand animals eat you.

443
00:45:23,880 --> 00:45:26,679
It seems the pain of your wound...

444
00:45:26,960 --> 00:45:29,279
...didn't bring you around.

445
00:45:31,880 --> 00:45:33,599
I swear..

446
00:45:33,720 --> 00:45:38,839
...I will make a wound in your
chest and cauterize it with salt!

447
00:45:44,360 --> 00:45:46,359
Are you only this strong?

448
00:45:46,600 --> 00:45:49,159
Hit me like a real man!

449
00:45:58,760 --> 00:46:00,639
Call reinforcements.

450
00:46:01,080 --> 00:46:03,639
We will need them thanks to Beys.

451
00:46:15,120 --> 00:46:17,119
Do you think...

452
00:46:17,400 --> 00:46:21,239
...we drew Osman Bey into a
trap by sending the messenger?

453
00:46:25,600 --> 00:46:29,119
Beys, I have an offer for you.

454
00:46:32,880 --> 00:46:36,159
But let's relax a bit first. Get them up.

455
00:46:59,840 --> 00:47:03,639
It seems your people aren't pleased
with our agreement, Osman Bey.

456
00:47:03,840 --> 00:47:05,359
Neither am I.

457
00:47:06,000 --> 00:47:10,399
Yet this isn't the first time
the wolf works with a jackal.

458
00:47:10,560 --> 00:47:14,239
There isn't only an agreement
but also Poena between us now.

459
00:47:14,440 --> 00:47:17,359
You have no relations left with Halime's past.

460
00:47:18,640 --> 00:47:23,519
When we take care of Mongolians,
we will see what happens.

461
00:47:24,440 --> 00:47:26,759
I looked after her for 10 years.

462
00:47:27,360 --> 00:47:29,439
There is a bond between me and her.

463
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:31,879
You can't change the past.

464
00:47:43,080 --> 00:47:47,159
Before I leave, I want to see Poena.

465
00:47:50,120 --> 00:47:54,399
They will look at Poena with
hatred. You can't change that.

466
00:47:55,240 --> 00:47:58,079
She will be upset and sad.

467
00:48:00,520 --> 00:48:02,879
You don't know what family means, Sofia.

468
00:48:03,040 --> 00:48:07,719
We will heal together all the wounds you opened.

469
00:48:08,120 --> 00:48:10,439
Halime will be even happier than before.

470
00:48:12,880 --> 00:48:16,199
Is that why your brother Alaaddin left?

471
00:48:25,760 --> 00:48:28,159
Poena will want to leave too.

472
00:48:28,520 --> 00:48:32,199
Then you will have to let her come to me.

473
00:48:33,920 --> 00:48:35,599
Look at me.

474
00:48:35,960 --> 00:48:39,399
If you mention taking Halime away,

475
00:48:39,720 --> 00:48:43,679
...I won't mind any agreements
but kill you right here.

476
00:48:49,320 --> 00:48:52,479
Fatma, how is your sister doing?

477
00:48:54,440 --> 00:48:56,959
Do you mean Sofia's daughter, father?

478
00:49:01,520 --> 00:49:04,759
She's fine. She will be alright.

479
00:49:08,280 --> 00:49:13,759
Reconsider what I said, Osman.

480
00:49:22,840 --> 00:49:24,399
Osman.

481
00:49:32,720 --> 00:49:36,279
-What is she doing here?
-Where is Poena?

482
00:50:15,040 --> 00:50:16,319
Halime.

483
00:50:18,040 --> 00:50:20,839
-My dear.
-My dear.

484
00:50:22,200 --> 00:50:25,199
Come. Come here.

485
00:50:25,480 --> 00:50:27,039
Come to me.

486
00:50:28,520 --> 00:50:30,399
Praise be.

487
00:50:30,720 --> 00:50:32,079
Praise be to you.

488
00:50:32,240 --> 00:50:34,079
You look great.

489
00:50:37,600 --> 00:50:40,079
You look perfect.

490
00:50:42,880 --> 00:50:45,759
Seeing you in my mother's clothes...

491
00:50:46,440 --> 00:50:48,359
You really look like her.

492
00:50:53,520 --> 00:50:59,039
My dear, they hid the
truth from both you and us.

493
00:50:59,720 --> 00:51:03,439
You're back to your family now. You are reborn.

494
00:51:05,720 --> 00:51:07,319
Huh, my pretty daughter?

495
00:51:08,800 --> 00:51:10,159
Poena.

496
00:51:15,560 --> 00:51:18,759
I'm here to say goodbye.

497
00:51:20,720 --> 00:51:23,479
Seeing you here like this...

498
00:51:25,320 --> 00:51:27,439
...is torturing me.

499
00:51:33,960 --> 00:51:35,319
Poena.

500
00:51:37,800 --> 00:51:41,759
-You won't be happy here.
-Shut up before I cut off your forked tongue.

501
00:51:48,720 --> 00:51:50,399
Alright.

502
00:51:53,720 --> 00:51:55,039
Alright.

503
00:51:56,800 --> 00:51:58,759
She's yours now, Bala.

504
00:52:04,560 --> 00:52:05,759
But..

505
00:52:09,560 --> 00:52:12,547
If she wants to leave one
day like your son Alaaddin...

506
00:52:12,559 --> 00:52:13,559
Enough!

507
00:52:14,240 --> 00:52:15,639
Shut up!

508
00:52:17,560 --> 00:52:20,839
I just care about Poena, Osman Bey.

509
00:52:21,360 --> 00:52:24,199
If she wants to leave one day, then...

510
00:52:25,960 --> 00:52:28,759
You will let her...

511
00:52:33,520 --> 00:52:34,999
..come back to me, her home.

512
00:52:35,080 --> 00:52:36,559
Her name is Halime.

513
00:52:36,720 --> 00:52:37,879
And her home is here.

514
00:52:38,120 --> 00:52:39,639
Stop dreaming, Sofia.

515
00:52:39,640 --> 00:52:42,399
What you say doesn't matter at all.

516
00:52:42,520 --> 00:52:45,319
-It's what Poena wants.
-Enough!

517
00:52:46,800 --> 00:52:49,279
Enough! My name isn't Poena.

518
00:52:53,720 --> 00:52:55,119
It's not Halime either.

519
00:52:58,760 --> 00:53:00,639
I don't know who I am.

520
00:53:02,040 --> 00:53:03,839
I don't know.

521
00:53:04,280 --> 00:53:05,599
I'm tired.

522
00:53:05,920 --> 00:53:07,759
I'm exhausted.

523
00:53:08,640 --> 00:53:12,599
Come here, my dear. Come here.

524
00:53:12,720 --> 00:53:14,199
Come.

525
00:53:20,400 --> 00:53:22,879
Get out. Out!

526
00:53:32,280 --> 00:53:34,159
Alright, Poena.

527
00:53:37,720 --> 00:53:40,399
Calm down, my dear. Calm down.

528
00:53:40,960 --> 00:53:43,839
It's alright now.
Have some rest now.

529
00:53:44,080 --> 00:53:45,559
Have some rest.

530
00:53:46,560 --> 00:53:48,199
Do I have permission, my Bey?

531
00:53:48,560 --> 00:53:49,679
Come in.

532
00:53:53,560 --> 00:53:56,319
My Bey, a messenger from Byzantine is here.

533
00:54:21,320 --> 00:54:22,759
Hristo, what's going on?

534
00:54:22,840 --> 00:54:26,559
Mongolian armies have come
near Ankara in huge numbers.

535
00:54:28,880 --> 00:54:32,799
Osman Bey, what do you think? Can we fight?

536
00:54:33,280 --> 00:54:35,759
We fought against the huge many times.

537
00:54:36,960 --> 00:54:38,399
What matter is..

538
00:54:38,800 --> 00:54:41,079
Just do what our alliance requires.

539
00:54:42,040 --> 00:54:42,959
Good.

540
00:54:43,480 --> 00:54:46,319
I was about to remind you of our alliance.

541
00:54:48,200 --> 00:54:50,959
We have a common enemy now.

542
00:54:58,200 --> 00:54:59,559
Osman Bey.

543
00:55:01,600 --> 00:55:03,599
Take care of my Poena.

544
00:55:04,400 --> 00:55:05,679
Look at me.

545
00:55:07,200 --> 00:55:09,159
If you don't want to be harmed

546
00:55:09,360 --> 00:55:11,639
...watch your forked tongue.

547
00:55:28,240 --> 00:55:29,799
Say it, Cerkutay.

548
00:55:30,720 --> 00:55:32,679
We have more information, my Bey.

549
00:55:36,320 --> 00:55:39,199
Mongolians are coming
to the frontiers in two corps.

550
00:55:39,440 --> 00:55:44,319
One is marching in the north of
Ankara and the other one in the south.

551
00:55:51,000 --> 00:55:54,839
It means they are marching
towards both Bursa and us, huh?

552
00:55:57,240 --> 00:56:02,919
My Bey, even if we prove that
Sofia killed Olcaytu's children,

553
00:56:03,520 --> 00:56:06,079
...their armies won't go back.

554
00:56:06,400 --> 00:56:09,479
If they come to the frontiers
it will cause destruction.

555
00:56:09,880 --> 00:56:14,799
Obviously, they intend to capture our lands.

556
00:56:14,800 --> 00:56:17,719
Capturing lands is just an opportunity for them.

557
00:56:17,760 --> 00:56:19,599
Olcaytu...

558
00:56:19,960 --> 00:56:23,679
He seeks vengeance. He
wants my children's blood.

559
00:56:23,880 --> 00:56:26,079
We will take more measures, my Bey.

560
00:56:26,200 --> 00:56:29,439
Neither Fatma nor Halime
will leave the tribe for a while.

561
00:56:41,840 --> 00:56:44,639
Alaeddin... Ah Alaeddin ah...

562
00:56:47,080 --> 00:56:49,639
He set out alone.

563
00:56:50,160 --> 00:56:52,439
Now his life may be in danger.

564
00:56:52,640 --> 00:56:53,799
-Kanyumaz.
-Yes my Bey.

565
00:56:53,800 --> 00:56:55,639
Go after him with the tracker Alps.

566
00:56:55,640 --> 00:56:57,199
As you order, my Bey.

567
00:57:05,800 --> 00:57:07,919
You caused division.

568
00:57:07,920 --> 00:57:11,559
Even though today is a celebration for us...

569
00:57:11,560 --> 00:57:14,199
...I can't even be happy
about the arrival of my child.

570
00:57:46,600 --> 00:57:48,799
I think this is enough.

571
00:57:50,200 --> 00:57:53,639
I am offering you something.

572
00:57:55,880 --> 00:57:59,479
Don't waste your poison.

573
00:58:06,640 --> 00:58:10,079
I will set you free and leave
you alive under one condition.

574
00:58:11,960 --> 00:58:15,479
You will pull your men back
from the Derince outpost.

575
00:58:15,480 --> 00:58:19,959
And you will allow my troops to enter there.

576
00:58:20,360 --> 00:58:24,359
So you want the land that
has become Turkish land?

577
00:58:25,800 --> 00:58:28,679
Did you hear that Hasan brother?

578
00:58:28,760 --> 00:58:31,319
He wants that land from us.

579
00:58:41,000 --> 00:58:46,919
Did you think we are those
who sell their honor for their lives?

580
00:58:52,040 --> 00:58:54,399
Then there will be no easy death for you.

581
00:59:03,760 --> 00:59:07,799
Will these blows defeat us, brother Hasan?

582
00:59:08,880 --> 00:59:11,759
They won't, old man.

583
00:59:17,440 --> 00:59:19,639
What did our ancestors say?

584
00:59:19,640 --> 00:59:22,439
Stand tall.

585
00:59:25,440 --> 00:59:31,839
"The horse knows the weight
of a man" they said, old man.

586
00:59:35,120 --> 00:59:36,999
"The mule..

587
00:59:37,440 --> 00:59:42,399
"The mule knows the burden
of heavy goods" they said.

588
00:59:45,360 --> 00:59:50,479
"Wherever there is pain, the one
who bears it knows it" they said.

589
00:59:51,320 --> 00:59:56,239
"Mindless heads suffer because of carelessness.

590
00:59:56,800 --> 01:00:01,959
Your mindless head will suffer
because of your carelessness.

591
01:00:01,960 --> 01:00:04,959
You infidel.

592
01:00:06,840 --> 01:00:07,919
Tie them

593
01:00:27,920 --> 01:00:37,399
I threw an apple and it rolled...

594
01:00:40,640 --> 01:00:47,679
It went and leaned against the cradle.

595
01:00:47,680 --> 01:00:53,079
The baby woke up from sleep.

596
01:00:53,080 --> 01:00:56,759
Lullaby, my daughter, my daughter.

597
01:00:56,760 --> 01:01:00,279
Lullaby, my child, my child.

598
01:01:00,280 --> 01:01:03,759
Lullaby, my baby, my baby.

599
01:01:03,760 --> 01:01:06,959
Lullaby, my dear, my dear.

600
01:01:06,960 --> 01:01:11,719
Lullaby, my baby.

601
01:01:15,080 --> 01:01:21,439
I couldn't call you "my baby".

602
01:01:22,120 --> 01:01:28,599
I couldn't hug you and kiss you.

603
01:01:28,800 --> 01:01:31,599
Lullaby, my child, my child.

604
01:01:31,600 --> 01:01:35,679
Lullaby, my daughter, my daughter.

605
01:01:35,720 --> 01:01:38,439
Lullaby, my baby, my baby.

606
01:01:38,440 --> 01:01:41,799
Lullaby, my dear, my dear.

607
01:02:21,160 --> 01:02:27,479
I said wrong things out of pain and anger.

608
01:02:28,520 --> 01:02:31,679
But again, you were right.

609
01:02:33,360 --> 01:02:37,479
Being right can cause pain sometimes.

610
01:02:38,800 --> 01:02:40,839
Even if you are a Bey.

611
01:02:43,880 --> 01:02:46,799
Can you forgive me. Dark Osman?

612
01:02:47,920 --> 01:02:50,119
So mothers can be devastated.

613
01:02:55,680 --> 01:02:58,439
Surely, even mothers can be devastated.

614
01:03:01,120 --> 01:03:03,719
But what's important is...

615
01:03:04,160 --> 01:03:08,799
...to stand together, supporting
each other, right, my Bala?

616
01:03:08,800 --> 01:03:10,239
That's right.

617
01:03:13,520 --> 01:03:16,079
We've been through many tests.

618
01:03:16,560 --> 01:03:19,159
The fire that burned our hearts has gone out.

619
01:03:19,160 --> 01:03:21,879
Here is where our heart's fire rests.

620
01:03:26,280 --> 01:03:30,159
I still can't believe it. It feels like a dream.

621
01:03:30,160 --> 01:03:32,559
All this time, she was right here.

622
01:03:33,120 --> 01:03:37,879
The first day I saw her, she looked
as if she would ease all my pain.

623
01:03:38,200 --> 01:03:40,399
But how did I not recognize her?

624
01:03:41,320 --> 01:03:44,119
I don't understand either. How did it happen?

625
01:03:44,120 --> 01:03:48,599
We always listened to the voice of
our hearts. How didn't we notice her?

626
01:03:48,600 --> 01:03:51,039
She came, sat at our table.

627
01:03:51,640 --> 01:03:54,039
We were together before.

628
01:03:54,040 --> 01:03:57,279
But no. From now on..

629
01:03:57,880 --> 01:04:02,319
...we will always be together, all together.
-All together?

630
01:04:03,520 --> 01:04:07,079
What about Alaeddin? What
if something happens to him?

631
01:04:07,080 --> 01:04:09,679
I sent Kanyumaz.

632
01:04:10,560 --> 01:04:12,479
The Alps will find him.

633
01:04:17,280 --> 01:04:20,199
Enough now. No more crying.

634
01:04:20,200 --> 01:04:22,559
Come here. Enough now.

635
01:04:22,560 --> 01:04:27,439
Look, we found Halime
too. The longing is over now.

636
01:04:38,640 --> 01:04:43,679
The Mongols will come from one side to Bursa
and from the other side directly to us.

637
01:04:43,760 --> 01:04:47,559
It wouldn't be right to split
our forces and try to stop them.

638
01:04:50,280 --> 01:04:55,119
Are you saying that we will join forces with
Sofia and get into the battle together, my Bey?

639
01:04:55,440 --> 01:04:57,399
Right. Right.

640
01:04:59,160 --> 01:05:02,599
We will unite with the Byzantine soldiers.

641
01:05:04,680 --> 01:05:10,199
When the Mongols split into two
forces, we must gather them in one place.

642
01:05:10,200 --> 01:05:14,919
That's why we'll move together
with the Byzantine soldiers.

643
01:05:15,920 --> 01:05:20,919
My Bey, the Byzantine soldiers
are not familiar with our army's order.

644
01:05:20,920 --> 01:05:24,199
Their armor is heavy, and their mobility is low.

645
01:05:24,200 --> 01:05:28,319
It will be difficult to fight
together with them in an order.

646
01:05:28,320 --> 01:05:29,959
You are right.

647
01:05:30,280 --> 01:05:35,399
That's why we need to train
them according to our army's order.

648
01:05:36,440 --> 01:05:38,239
This duty is yours.

649
01:05:38,240 --> 01:05:40,799
As you order, my Bey.

650
01:05:41,080 --> 01:05:42,439
My Bey.

651
01:05:44,160 --> 01:05:48,039
What if that snake Sofia plays a game again?

652
01:05:48,640 --> 01:05:49,839
No.

653
01:05:49,840 --> 01:05:54,719
As long as the Mongol threat is
here, Sofia cannot break the alliance.

654
01:05:56,240 --> 01:05:58,879
If she tries to break the alliance...

655
01:05:59,160 --> 01:06:01,719
...she knows very well that she will lose Bursa.

656
01:06:05,040 --> 01:06:08,959
But after we get rid of the Mongol threat...

657
01:06:08,960 --> 01:06:11,599
...she knows that our
swords will turn against her.

658
01:06:11,600 --> 01:06:15,039
That's why we must be careful.

659
01:06:15,040 --> 01:06:16,839
Okay my Bey.

660
01:06:19,000 --> 01:06:21,399
The Claudius dog

661
01:06:26,200 --> 01:06:29,639
I wonder why he opposes this alliance.

662
01:06:32,120 --> 01:06:34,319
He came to defend Bursa.

663
01:06:35,400 --> 01:06:40,559
But sooner or later, we will
understand what his intention is.

664
01:06:43,040 --> 01:06:44,599
Koca Bey, Hasan Bey.

665
01:06:44,600 --> 01:06:45,839
They left a while ago.

666
01:06:45,840 --> 01:06:48,679
What is their situation?
Haven't we received news?

667
01:06:48,680 --> 01:06:51,239
No news yet, my Bey.

668
01:07:16,440 --> 01:07:18,039
My Poena.

669
01:07:18,120 --> 01:07:19,999
My little bird.

670
01:07:25,400 --> 01:07:27,239
My little bird.

671
01:07:30,480 --> 01:07:33,999
I left my heart with you
for the future of Bursa.

672
01:07:38,600 --> 01:07:40,119
Sofia.

673
01:07:41,080 --> 01:07:43,199
Have you learned where he is?

674
01:07:44,560 --> 01:07:48,639
Claudius took his soldiers and left Bursa.

675
01:07:54,160 --> 01:07:56,119
Claudius.

676
01:07:57,600 --> 01:08:00,959
You leave me no choice but to kill you.

677
01:08:06,240 --> 01:08:07,039
Hristo.

678
01:08:10,200 --> 01:08:16,399
You will find that fool
before he ruins my plans.

679
01:08:17,600 --> 01:08:20,037
Would he oppose the emperor's decision?

680
01:08:20,040 --> 01:08:23,679
He carries the heart of a devil, Hristo.

681
01:08:24,040 --> 01:08:29,439
He does whatever he has in mind, no matter what.

682
01:08:30,520 --> 01:08:33,158
I'm sure he is trying to do something.

683
01:08:37,960 --> 01:08:39,839
But I will learn this...

684
01:08:41,439 --> 01:08:45,078
...and stop him from breaking the alliance.

685
01:08:53,000 --> 01:08:54,559
My sister...

686
01:08:56,080 --> 01:08:59,759
...was right next to us all this time.

687
01:09:00,880 --> 01:09:04,037
Alaeddin would be very
happy if he were here now.

688
01:09:08,800 --> 01:09:10,479
But Alaeddin...

689
01:09:13,560 --> 01:09:17,278
Alaeddin chose to leave us.

690
01:09:24,359 --> 01:09:25,919
Holofira.

691
01:09:32,240 --> 01:09:33,799
Holofira.

692
01:09:36,640 --> 01:09:38,519
Lord's daughter.

693
01:09:40,359 --> 01:09:42,158
Are you alright?

694
01:09:45,279 --> 01:09:46,759
Orhan..

695
01:09:49,319 --> 01:09:52,198
I guess I'm facing myself.

696
01:09:54,200 --> 01:09:59,479
I've actually been searching
for myself for a long time.

697
01:10:02,320 --> 01:10:07,039
Do you remember when
Yunus Emre told us about love?

698
01:10:07,240 --> 01:10:09,199
I remember.

699
01:10:09,680 --> 01:10:11,999
I never forgot.

700
01:10:14,680 --> 01:10:19,759
I thought it was only the love I felt for you.

701
01:10:20,480 --> 01:10:24,319
But there was another love in it.

702
01:10:32,080 --> 01:10:35,599
When this love has fallen into my heart...

703
01:10:36,360 --> 01:10:39,119
...I can't wear this necklace anymore.

704
01:10:45,920 --> 01:10:48,479
My Holofira.

705
01:10:49,000 --> 01:10:50,639
My beautiful wife...

706
01:10:52,920 --> 01:10:54,319
Orhan.

707
01:10:58,280 --> 01:11:00,839
...want to be Muslim.

708
01:11:09,000 --> 01:11:11,879
You gave me the world.

709
01:11:17,840 --> 01:11:20,079
My Hatun..

710
01:11:21,560 --> 01:11:23,759
loved one...

711
01:11:25,120 --> 01:11:26,679
May my Allah...

712
01:11:28,160 --> 01:11:30,719
May my Allah keep us together...

713
01:11:31,920 --> 01:11:35,239
...in both worlds, God willing.

714
01:11:37,640 --> 01:11:38,959
Aameen.

715
01:11:50,240 --> 01:11:51,799
Come, my daughter.

716
01:11:51,920 --> 01:11:55,959
Ulgen Hatun is preparing the meals you love.

717
01:11:55,960 --> 01:11:58,039
Thank you Bala Hatun.

718
01:12:00,200 --> 01:12:02,599
Won't you call me mother?

719
01:12:04,040 --> 01:12:06,159
It is not easy for me.

720
01:12:08,040 --> 01:12:12,359
I thought you were my enemy a while ago.

721
01:12:13,680 --> 01:12:15,359
Wait..

722
01:12:15,760 --> 01:12:17,359
Wait...

723
01:12:17,600 --> 01:12:21,439
She will say this word when the time comes.

724
01:12:21,440 --> 01:12:24,599
Right, my beautiful daughter?

725
01:12:24,600 --> 01:12:28,039
You can call me that whenever you want.

726
01:12:29,000 --> 01:12:31,639
I still don't understand.

727
01:12:31,920 --> 01:12:33,639
How can you trust me?

728
01:12:33,640 --> 01:12:35,759
Your essence is real and strong.

729
01:12:37,080 --> 01:12:42,199
Even when you were our
enemy, did you only do bad things?

730
01:12:43,640 --> 01:12:48,199
Even if your mind told you
so, your heart didn't allow it.

731
01:12:50,320 --> 01:12:54,079
You turned back from many mistakes.

732
01:12:55,360 --> 01:12:56,639
Right.

733
01:12:56,640 --> 01:13:01,799
You told Sofia the location of the secret
tribe, but then you came and informed us.

734
01:13:01,800 --> 01:13:03,079
Remember the cave?

735
01:13:03,280 --> 01:13:05,679
When I drew my sword against the infidels...

736
01:13:05,720 --> 01:13:08,239
..you followed and fought against them with me.

737
01:13:08,240 --> 01:13:11,959
You didn't leave me alone.
You didn't leave me there.

738
01:13:12,320 --> 01:13:14,679
Could a traitor do this?

739
01:13:14,680 --> 01:13:18,839
Maybe you knew more, but you didn't tell Sofia.

740
01:13:19,280 --> 01:13:23,759
In fact, you even drew
your sword against Sofia...

741
01:13:23,920 --> 01:13:26,599
...and saved Holofira and her baby.

742
01:13:27,280 --> 01:13:30,439
Look, people make mistakes.

743
01:13:30,480 --> 01:13:32,199
That's the nature of people.

744
01:13:32,200 --> 01:13:37,159
But what's important is that you turn back
from your mistake. Alright, my daughter?

745
01:13:39,880 --> 01:13:41,439
Look...

746
01:13:43,720 --> 01:13:45,559
This was yours.

747
01:13:46,000 --> 01:13:48,079
This brought you to me.

748
01:13:49,880 --> 01:13:52,359
Now it will protect you again, huh?

749
01:13:54,720 --> 01:13:57,559
Come on now, you will pour the sherbets today.

750
01:13:57,560 --> 01:14:02,439
Her father wants his daughter
to pour him sherbet, huh?

751
01:14:05,600 --> 01:14:07,519
Praise be.

752
01:14:15,720 --> 01:14:20,479
I wonder what they fed my
little daughter in that devil's den.

753
01:14:21,240 --> 01:14:28,439
But now with my meals, both her
mind and her heart will find their way.

754
01:14:28,800 --> 01:14:32,439
Her soul was cooked in the devil's temple.

755
01:14:32,720 --> 01:14:36,679
What will these meals do? I
hope she doesn't spread discord again.

756
01:14:36,680 --> 01:14:38,359
My Fatma!

757
01:14:42,200 --> 01:14:47,759
Ulgen Hatun, there's a
fake happiness in the tribe.

758
01:14:50,440 --> 01:14:53,039
But it will just cause a disaster.

759
01:14:53,560 --> 01:14:58,559
What that girl has done
is clear. I don't trust her.

760
01:14:59,440 --> 01:15:01,479
I understand you.

761
01:15:02,680 --> 01:15:04,639
Fatma Hatun.

762
01:15:05,640 --> 01:15:07,439
But she's your sister.

763
01:15:07,440 --> 01:15:08,879
My sister?

764
01:15:08,880 --> 01:15:12,839
When I look at her, I see a traitor
who spreads lies and plans games.

765
01:15:13,240 --> 01:15:15,279
Don't say that. Don't say that.

766
01:15:15,280 --> 01:15:16,919
Look at me.

767
01:15:17,120 --> 01:15:19,799
Don't do something crazy at the table.

768
01:15:21,000 --> 01:15:22,679
Don't, my Fatma.

769
01:15:52,520 --> 01:15:55,919
Tell me. What do you want from us?

770
01:15:58,720 --> 01:16:00,719
Under my rule...

771
01:16:01,000 --> 01:16:07,199
...a Shahzade and his
Hatun cannot eat dry bread.

772
01:16:07,560 --> 01:16:11,439
This is not possible. Come to the table.

773
01:16:11,440 --> 01:16:12,839
No.

774
01:16:13,680 --> 01:16:15,999
Your food is forbidden for us.

775
01:16:41,160 --> 01:16:45,279
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

776
01:16:50,320 --> 01:16:52,119
Enjoy.

777
01:17:07,720 --> 01:17:09,199
So you say..

778
01:17:10,440 --> 01:17:16,199
"I am a scholar, I know the
special written works." huh?

779
01:17:16,480 --> 01:17:18,279
Bey's son.

780
01:17:21,160 --> 01:17:23,079
"Justice..

781
01:17:25,120 --> 01:17:29,159
...no matter what stands against him...

782
01:17:29,160 --> 01:17:36,839
..is crushing everything that stands in
the way of a person's path" says Farabi.

783
01:17:41,240 --> 01:17:46,119
Was he wrong about this?

784
01:17:46,680 --> 01:17:48,239
With this saying...

785
01:17:48,720 --> 01:17:53,839
...didn't he describe the Mongol
who flows like a flood across the world?

786
01:17:54,160 --> 01:17:55,799
Tell me.

787
01:17:58,320 --> 01:18:00,599
The one who said it is right.

788
01:18:00,600 --> 01:18:04,519
But the one who understood it this way is wrong.

789
01:18:05,800 --> 01:18:08,679
You surely know this well.

790
01:18:09,560 --> 01:18:15,679
You interpret Farabi's words in
a way that suits your interests.

791
01:18:17,560 --> 01:18:21,119
If you don't like our interpretation...

792
01:18:22,280 --> 01:18:24,879
...then tell us what it means.

793
01:18:33,320 --> 01:18:36,199
With this saying Farabi meant...

794
01:18:37,520 --> 01:18:41,639
...the justice in an ignorant city.

795
01:18:44,840 --> 01:18:46,359
So...

796
01:18:47,560 --> 01:18:51,119
Tell me how to be suitably fair then.

797
01:18:51,800 --> 01:18:53,799
Let me say it...

798
01:18:54,360 --> 01:18:57,079
...and you understand it well.

799
01:18:57,840 --> 01:19:03,159
Being fair is not invading
lands like Mongols like a flood...

800
01:19:03,160 --> 01:19:07,079
...turning every place
into a desert and leaving.

801
01:19:08,920 --> 01:19:11,279
Being fair is, Kucar...

802
01:19:13,560 --> 01:19:18,399
..improving those deserts
and bringing abundance.

803
01:19:35,040 --> 01:19:36,759
It's a pity.

804
01:19:38,960 --> 01:19:40,519
Osman..

805
01:19:41,480 --> 01:19:47,919
...will lose a shahzade whose
mind is sharper than a sword like you.

806
01:19:50,040 --> 01:19:51,759
What a pity!

807
01:20:07,520 --> 01:20:13,439
Halime, you're back and
our table is more joyful now.

808
01:20:16,120 --> 01:20:18,279
I don't remember much, but...

809
01:20:18,720 --> 01:20:22,599
...I've always envied such tables.

810
01:20:24,360 --> 01:20:26,759
Crowded and warm.

811
01:20:28,840 --> 01:20:30,519
I used to dream.

812
01:20:31,800 --> 01:20:34,319
Dreaming leads to reality, my dear.

813
01:20:34,600 --> 01:20:37,799
We went through a lot but it's alright now.

814
01:20:38,240 --> 01:20:41,119
We will have nice days. Right, Halime?

815
01:20:44,000 --> 01:20:46,039
Halime is back.

816
01:20:47,760 --> 01:20:50,359
Alaaddin will be back too. I know that.

817
01:20:51,160 --> 01:20:55,719
Ulgen, put Alaaddin's and
Gonca's plates on the table.

818
01:20:56,240 --> 01:20:59,879
I want them to see they always
have a place here when they are back.

819
01:21:09,720 --> 01:21:11,359
Do I have permission, my Bey?

820
01:21:16,000 --> 01:21:17,799
Come in.

821
01:21:33,240 --> 01:21:34,999
Join us.

822
01:21:43,640 --> 01:21:45,919
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

823
01:21:56,400 --> 01:21:57,959
Let's get started.

824
01:21:58,760 --> 01:22:00,839
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

825
01:22:01,000 --> 01:22:02,959
Let's eat.

826
01:22:03,520 --> 01:22:05,999
Okay, my Bey.

827
01:22:07,480 --> 01:22:12,879
Well... Father. Mother.

828
01:22:14,080 --> 01:22:16,399
Before we start eating.

829
01:22:17,480 --> 01:22:23,159
...Holofira has important news to tell you.

830
01:22:32,840 --> 01:22:35,959
I didn't think I would be so excited.

831
01:22:40,440 --> 01:22:42,879
It's obviously happy news.

832
01:22:44,680 --> 01:22:46,719
Don't make us curious, my dear.

833
01:22:57,360 --> 01:22:59,799
If you approve.

834
01:23:01,520 --> 01:23:04,599
..I want to become a Muslim.

835
01:23:12,720 --> 01:23:14,399
Well..

836
01:23:34,760 --> 01:23:38,519
Alaaddin, that's why you
joined that demon's table, huh?

837
01:23:43,760 --> 01:23:44,959
Tell me.

838
01:23:45,520 --> 01:23:48,839
Will the oil around your
wrists help you untie the ropes?

839
01:23:50,320 --> 01:23:51,879
It will, Gonca.

840
01:23:52,320 --> 01:23:53,599
It needs to help.

841
01:23:53,840 --> 01:23:55,799
It has to.

842
01:23:56,200 --> 01:23:58,399
Keep your eyes on that demon.

843
01:23:58,880 --> 01:24:02,239
-Almost done.
-What are you saying? Stop nagging.

844
01:24:07,400 --> 01:24:09,999
-Come on, come on.
-Is it untied?

845
01:24:10,160 --> 01:24:12,639
Come on.

846
01:24:15,280 --> 01:24:17,759
Thanks to Allah, it's untied.

847
01:24:20,400 --> 01:24:23,199
Alaaddin, his back is turned.

848
01:24:45,680 --> 01:24:50,079
-I got it.
-Come here, hatun.

849
01:24:54,120 --> 01:24:57,319
We have to hurry. Come on.

850
01:24:57,480 --> 01:25:01,399
-Come on. Alaaddin.
-I'm trying.

851
01:25:04,160 --> 01:25:05,399
Come on.

852
01:25:05,560 --> 01:25:08,679
Let's get out of this jackal's
den before they see us.

853
01:25:20,680 --> 01:25:22,879
Come on, come on.

854
01:25:29,960 --> 01:25:32,679
Let's go. Come here, hatun.

855
01:25:33,920 --> 01:25:35,999
I heard a cracking sound. Get down.

856
01:25:48,200 --> 01:25:50,879
Let's go, my dear. Come on.

857
01:25:58,400 --> 01:26:00,239
Come on.

858
01:26:01,320 --> 01:26:02,919
Prisoners are escaping!

859
01:26:10,720 --> 01:26:12,839
-Alaaddin, come on.
-Come on.

860
01:26:16,080 --> 01:26:19,759
Alaaddin! Alaaddin

861
01:26:20,360 --> 01:26:22,279
They can never run away!

862
01:26:22,360 --> 01:26:25,399
-Catch them!
-Nokers, catch!

863
01:26:26,800 --> 01:26:28,159
Hurry, run!

864
01:26:35,800 --> 01:26:37,039
Run, hatun!

865
01:26:39,160 --> 01:26:41,319
Alaaddin, wait. Your wound...

866
01:26:41,480 --> 01:26:44,439
-It's not a big deal. Come on, run!
-Alaaddin.

867
01:26:47,400 --> 01:26:49,479
They're running off. Let's catch them.

868
01:26:49,640 --> 01:26:51,279
They're sending a signal.

869
01:26:51,280 --> 01:26:53,719
It seems there are soldiers where we are going.

870
01:26:53,960 --> 01:26:56,399
This way, Gonca. Come on, hatun!

871
01:26:56,600 --> 01:26:59,319
Peace be upon you.

872
01:26:59,760 --> 01:27:03,519
You beat these ones. I will
slaughter the ones in the back.

873
01:27:16,880 --> 01:27:18,399
Gonca

874
01:27:21,200 --> 01:27:23,879
Drop your sword now or she will die.

875
01:27:25,920 --> 01:27:28,719
Alright. I'm putting it down.

876
01:27:29,360 --> 01:27:31,479
Don't do anything crazy.

877
01:27:39,640 --> 01:27:41,519
Keep calm.

878
01:27:48,320 --> 01:27:49,879
Alaaddin.

879
01:27:50,520 --> 01:27:52,759
Are you alright, Gonca?
-I'm fine.

880
01:27:53,000 --> 01:27:55,879
Come on then. We have to go

881
01:27:56,040 --> 01:27:58,399
-Alaaddin.
-Alaaddin, stop there!

882
01:27:59,040 --> 01:28:01,599
If you want to survive, stop!

883
01:28:05,720 --> 01:28:08,559
My dear, now repeat what I say.

884
01:28:12,800 --> 01:28:16,879
I bear witness that there is no god but Allah...

885
01:28:17,480 --> 01:28:20,839
I bear witness that there is no god but Allah...

886
01:28:21,800 --> 01:28:27,439
...and Muhammad is His messenger.

887
01:28:29,480 --> 01:28:34,759
...and Muhammad
is His messenger.

888
01:29:00,280 --> 01:29:02,359
May Allah make it sacred.

889
01:29:04,320 --> 01:29:06,759
-Aameen.
-Aameen.

890
01:29:23,040 --> 01:29:28,039
Now we need to give you a suitable name.

891
01:29:28,440 --> 01:29:32,559
In my dream, I was told 'you aren't Holofira'.

892
01:29:35,880 --> 01:29:38,159
And they put this mirror in my palm.

893
01:29:41,120 --> 01:29:42,799
This flower..

894
01:29:52,160 --> 01:29:56,159
You say so, huh?

895
01:29:58,400 --> 01:29:59,919
Nilufer (Lotus).

896
01:30:01,280 --> 01:30:02,559
Nilufer.

897
01:30:03,800 --> 01:30:06,279
The flower that blossoms in the marshland.

898
01:30:08,200 --> 01:30:12,639
You left the cruel and came here.

899
01:30:13,680 --> 01:30:16,559
You abandoned the evil.

900
01:30:18,600 --> 01:30:22,599
The love of Islam has arisen in your heart.

901
01:30:27,160 --> 01:30:30,199
Well... Then..

902
01:30:33,560 --> 01:30:36,039
The name which will suit you is...

903
01:30:38,320 --> 01:30:39,719
...Nilufer.

904
01:30:50,520 --> 01:30:54,599
May Allah give you a long life, father.

905
01:31:03,000 --> 01:31:07,279
May Allah let you be the neighbor
of our Prophet in heaven.

906
01:31:12,840 --> 01:31:14,879
Your name.

907
01:31:16,600 --> 01:31:18,359
..is Nilufer Hatun now.

908
01:31:22,480 --> 01:31:24,079
And this is..

909
01:31:24,680 --> 01:31:27,279
...a gift from me for Nilufer Hatun.

910
01:31:46,720 --> 01:31:48,519
I hope your enjoy it, my dear.

911
01:32:04,080 --> 01:32:05,559
Congratulations.

912
01:32:06,640 --> 01:32:08,319
It must be very hard.

913
01:32:11,200 --> 01:32:13,759
There is ease in every hardship.

914
01:32:14,440 --> 01:32:17,959
The truth is exposed for those who know that.

915
01:32:32,080 --> 01:32:33,399
My Bey.

916
01:32:35,040 --> 01:32:37,439
I want to tell you something.

917
01:32:38,120 --> 01:32:40,479
While I have this burden on me

918
01:32:41,440 --> 01:32:42,999
...I don't feel comfortable.

919
01:32:44,600 --> 01:32:46,039
Go ahead.

920
01:32:48,560 --> 01:32:50,119
Alaaddin Bey.

921
01:32:54,880 --> 01:32:59,279
It was a mistake that he left the
battlefield and insisted on his mistake.

922
01:33:00,120 --> 01:33:01,919
But I made a mistake too, my Bey.

923
01:33:02,800 --> 01:33:04,559
I was overwhelmed by my anger.

924
01:33:05,760 --> 01:33:08,959
-I hit my brother.
-What did you do?

925
01:33:10,600 --> 01:33:13,199
I told Alaaddin not to leave, my Bey.

926
01:33:13,720 --> 01:33:15,359
But he didn't mind.

927
01:33:19,400 --> 01:33:20,879
I didn't...

928
01:33:22,040 --> 01:33:24,239
...want this to happen.

929
01:33:24,520 --> 01:33:26,159
But it happened.

930
01:33:27,960 --> 01:33:29,359
Yes, my Bey.

931
01:33:30,280 --> 01:33:31,279
It happened.

932
01:33:32,440 --> 01:33:34,279
The mistake you two made...

933
01:33:35,600 --> 01:33:37,119
...was causing unrest.

934
01:33:41,240 --> 01:33:42,559
My Bey.

935
01:33:44,920 --> 01:33:47,519
While it isn't safe around...

936
01:33:48,440 --> 01:33:50,559
...and Kucar is in the frontiers

937
01:33:50,880 --> 01:33:52,519
..I'm worried about them.

938
01:33:52,600 --> 01:33:54,119
I know Alaaddin, my Bey.

939
01:33:54,280 --> 01:33:55,639
I know my brother.

940
01:33:55,680 --> 01:33:58,159
If I don't go after him

941
01:33:58,520 --> 01:34:00,439
...he will never come back.

942
01:34:06,520 --> 01:34:11,359
With your permission, I'd
like to go see my brother...

943
01:34:11,720 --> 01:34:13,719
...and settle the matter between us.

944
01:34:15,440 --> 01:34:21,679
I want my brother Alaaddin to
come back to his family and tribe.

945
01:34:28,560 --> 01:34:30,999
-Do I have permission, my Bey?
-Come in!

946
01:34:36,320 --> 01:34:40,639
My Bey, the dog called
Claudius played an evil trick.

947
01:34:41,520 --> 01:34:44,759
Hasan Bey and Koca Bey lost too many.

948
01:34:45,240 --> 01:34:47,759
-Where are they? -In Tavsantepe.

949
01:34:48,080 --> 01:34:51,319
They've retreated to defend
and are waiting for aid.

950
01:34:51,880 --> 01:34:53,279
Gather the alps.

951
01:34:54,120 --> 01:34:55,879
We'll go help them.

952
01:34:56,240 --> 01:34:57,519
As you order, my Bey.

953
01:35:01,520 --> 01:35:04,359
Fath... Osman Bey.

954
01:35:05,920 --> 01:35:07,559
Don't go.

955
01:35:08,160 --> 01:35:10,079
Claudius is a dangerous man.

956
01:35:10,320 --> 01:35:11,879
Don't worry.

957
01:35:12,200 --> 01:35:14,759
I will ruin Claudius' game.

958
01:35:16,400 --> 01:35:18,359
And then we will come back.

959
01:35:23,040 --> 01:35:24,759
My daughters and wife.

960
01:35:25,600 --> 01:35:27,839
They will defend our tribe.

961
01:35:30,520 --> 01:35:32,759
You go after Alaaddin.

962
01:35:34,120 --> 01:35:36,279
Only you can bring him back.

963
01:35:37,120 --> 01:35:38,639
As you order, my Bey.

964
01:35:45,600 --> 01:35:46,999
Kucar.

965
01:35:49,000 --> 01:35:51,439
He must have a plan.

966
01:35:52,400 --> 01:35:54,959
But we can't let him win.

967
01:35:56,440 --> 01:35:57,839
Let's go.

968
01:36:22,080 --> 01:36:24,559
Why are you looking, Scholar? Come here.

969
01:36:26,680 --> 01:36:29,639
We'll keep going after we change your bandage.
-No.

970
01:36:29,880 --> 01:36:31,999
It's just a little cut. Never mind.

971
01:36:32,320 --> 01:36:36,799
Gonca, my sister Halime... That
demon is going to abduct her.

972
01:36:37,200 --> 01:36:40,719
We shouldn't waste any more
time. We have to go. Come on.

973
01:36:41,240 --> 01:36:44,159
-Come on.
-Alaaddin.

974
01:36:51,920 --> 01:36:54,439
Vile dogs.

975
01:36:55,120 --> 01:36:57,439
You took our smell?

976
01:36:57,800 --> 01:37:00,719
Gonca, stand behind me.

977
01:37:01,080 --> 01:37:04,519
-Be careful.
-Do not resist, Shahzade Alaaddin.

978
01:37:04,960 --> 01:37:06,559
Drop your sword.

979
01:37:07,120 --> 01:37:11,639
If you don't care about
yourself, care about your wife.

980
01:37:13,240 --> 01:37:14,759
You dog.

981
01:37:17,280 --> 01:37:19,319
-Hatun!
-Alaaddin!

982
01:37:19,520 --> 01:37:21,159
Alaaddin

983
01:37:28,200 --> 01:37:29,639
Alaaddin.

984
01:37:29,760 --> 01:37:32,119
Get off!

985
01:37:33,320 --> 01:37:35,439
-Don't touch her!
-Alaaddin!

986
01:37:35,600 --> 01:37:38,759
-Alaaddin!
-Leave her! Leave her!

987
01:37:39,640 --> 01:37:42,639
Get off! Leave me!
-Leave her!

988
01:37:42,720 --> 01:37:44,039
Leave her!

989
01:37:44,720 --> 01:37:46,879
Can't you just fight bravely?

990
01:37:47,120 --> 01:37:50,239
If you have courage, fight me with your swords!

991
01:37:50,320 --> 01:37:52,559
-Vile dogs!
-Get off!

992
01:37:52,960 --> 01:37:56,399
Leave me and I will show
you what death smells like!

993
01:37:56,800 --> 01:38:02,639
Mongolians spreading death around
the world know what death smells like!

994
01:38:03,840 --> 01:38:06,879
-Hatun!
-You dog.

995
01:38:09,240 --> 01:38:11,919
You dog! Leave me!

996
01:38:12,200 --> 01:38:19,199
Apart from your captivity, you and
I had some friendship, Bey's son.

997
01:38:19,600 --> 01:38:23,079
But friendship is over.

998
01:38:24,360 --> 01:38:27,239
-Leave me!
-Don't worry.

999
01:38:27,840 --> 01:38:30,919
I will help you meet your sister Halime.

1000
01:38:31,080 --> 01:38:32,519
Kucar!

1001
01:38:32,760 --> 01:38:36,919
Leave my sister Halime alone! Let my wife go!

1002
01:38:37,040 --> 01:38:41,439
Be a real man and fight me. You vile dog!

1003
01:38:44,160 --> 01:38:47,679
Put them inside the cage! Now!

1004
01:38:47,960 --> 01:38:50,679
-Get off! Get off!
-You demon!

1005
01:38:50,720 --> 01:38:52,559
-Leave me.
-You demon.

1006
01:38:52,600 --> 01:38:55,399
-I'll kill all of you! All of you!
-Get off!

1007
01:38:55,920 --> 01:38:57,559
Get off!

1008
01:39:06,360 --> 01:39:08,319
I have a message from Claudius.

1009
01:39:14,280 --> 01:39:16,839
This is Claudius' messenger, Kucar.

1010
01:39:19,720 --> 01:39:21,719
Speak, little bird.

1011
01:39:21,720 --> 01:39:25,479
Claudius lured Osman
into a trap through the Beys.

1012
01:39:25,480 --> 01:39:26,359
Orlok Kucar..

1013
01:39:26,360 --> 01:39:28,119
...he is waiting for your support.

1014
01:39:28,120 --> 01:39:31,479
Where does he want us to support him?
-In Tavsantepe.

1015
01:39:31,640 --> 01:39:32,599
Excellent.

1016
01:39:33,960 --> 01:39:36,719
If Osman dies in this trap...

1017
01:39:36,720 --> 01:39:40,199
...the battle will end before it starts.

1018
01:39:40,200 --> 01:39:42,999
Then it will be Bursa's turn.

1019
01:39:47,320 --> 01:39:48,999
Nokers!

1020
01:39:49,000 --> 01:39:50,559
Come on!

1021
01:39:58,000 --> 01:40:03,119
No one will go anywhere alone
until we get rid of the Mongol threat.

1022
01:40:03,120 --> 01:40:04,839
Alright, my daughters?

1023
01:40:05,000 --> 01:40:07,839
God willing my brothers will come back safely.

1024
01:40:07,840 --> 01:40:08,999
God willing.

1025
01:40:09,000 --> 01:40:13,319
Bala Hatun, why did Alaeddin Bey leave?

1026
01:40:20,720 --> 01:40:22,599
Bala Hatun, huh?

1027
01:40:24,400 --> 01:40:26,559
You cannot even call her mother.

1028
01:40:27,520 --> 01:40:29,079
My Fatma.

1029
01:40:29,080 --> 01:40:30,399
Yes, mother?

1030
01:40:30,400 --> 01:40:32,439
She cannot even call you mother.

1031
01:40:32,440 --> 01:40:35,319
But she can call Sofia "aunt" easily.

1032
01:40:35,320 --> 01:40:38,159
Although she found out what she did!

1033
01:40:39,960 --> 01:40:41,359
My Fatma..

1034
01:40:41,360 --> 01:40:42,599
Now is not the time.

1035
01:40:42,600 --> 01:40:45,319
When will it be time, Ulgen sister?

1036
01:40:47,600 --> 01:40:51,719
So that you feel close to
Sofia, go and live with her!

1037
01:40:52,640 --> 01:40:54,359
I did not forgive her.

1038
01:40:54,360 --> 01:40:56,319
Forgive?

1039
01:40:56,360 --> 01:40:59,559
You should have killed her!

1040
01:41:03,240 --> 01:41:05,199
You cannot say "brother"...

1041
01:41:05,200 --> 01:41:07,519
...and you say "Alaeddin Bey

1042
01:41:07,760 --> 01:41:11,639
My brothers fell out with
each other because of you!

1043
01:41:12,320 --> 01:41:15,159
They fought because of Claudius!

1044
01:41:15,280 --> 01:41:17,199
Because of you...

1045
01:41:17,200 --> 01:41:19,159
...our family has fallen apart.

1046
01:41:19,320 --> 01:41:21,159
I am not one of them.

1047
01:41:21,160 --> 01:41:23,439
You are not one of them.

1048
01:41:23,440 --> 01:41:25,639
But you are not one of us either!

1049
01:41:25,640 --> 01:41:26,799
Fatma.

1050
01:41:26,800 --> 01:41:28,599
Stop it, my daughter.

1051
01:41:30,440 --> 01:41:33,679
This family cannot
overcome another sibling fight.

1052
01:41:35,360 --> 01:41:37,559
I don't have a sister, mother.

1053
01:41:40,280 --> 01:41:41,799
Fatma.

1054
01:41:45,360 --> 01:41:47,519
Fatma..

1055
01:41:54,160 --> 01:41:55,759
My Halime...

1056
01:41:57,080 --> 01:41:59,319
Don't be mad at your sister, alright?

1057
01:41:59,360 --> 01:42:02,879
She loved you very much, but now...
-She can't bear my betrayal.

1058
01:42:02,880 --> 01:42:04,159
Right?

1059
01:42:06,640 --> 01:42:08,839
She didn't think her sister could do that.

1060
01:42:08,840 --> 01:42:10,279
She is right.

1061
01:42:10,680 --> 01:42:12,439
I am a traitor.

1062
01:42:15,080 --> 01:42:16,999
Right, Ulgen Hatun?

1063
01:42:19,120 --> 01:42:20,639
I deceived everyone.

1064
01:42:20,720 --> 01:42:23,439
Could you trust me again if it was you?

1065
01:42:40,720 --> 01:42:43,459
Near Tavsantepe

1066
01:42:56,720 --> 01:42:58,119
My Bey.

1067
01:43:08,680 --> 01:43:10,559
Hasan Bey and...

1068
01:43:10,680 --> 01:43:12,919
...Koca Bey's Alps.

1069
01:43:15,080 --> 01:43:17,159
They killed him.

1070
01:43:17,360 --> 01:43:21,199
My Bey, when our valiants left the
outpost, their number was this many.

1071
01:43:21,960 --> 01:43:24,119
They all became martyrs.

1072
01:43:24,800 --> 01:43:25,759
My Bey.

1073
01:43:25,760 --> 01:43:28,359
Beys are not among the martyrs.

1074
01:43:28,640 --> 01:43:30,999
If they were defeated

1075
01:43:31,040 --> 01:43:33,359
...where are the Beys then, my Bey?

1076
01:44:00,000 --> 01:44:02,239
Turkmen scabbard...

1077
01:44:02,600 --> 01:44:04,599
It points to there.

1078
01:44:05,560 --> 01:44:07,759
They went this way.

1079
01:44:11,600 --> 01:44:13,439
But..

1080
01:44:14,040 --> 01:44:16,359
...infidels are after them.

1081
01:44:17,280 --> 01:44:20,439
But they didn't move quickly as we expected.

1082
01:44:20,680 --> 01:44:23,039
Do you think that's a trap, my Bey?

1083
01:44:25,440 --> 01:44:28,359
Claudius' goal is not killing the Beys.

1084
01:44:28,560 --> 01:44:32,839
His intention is to draw
them to the place he wants.

1085
01:44:33,720 --> 01:44:38,439
Claudius is moving contrary to what we expected.

1086
01:44:38,520 --> 01:44:43,279
Now I understand what your intention is.

1087
01:44:43,600 --> 01:44:48,999
Sofia... Sofia even gave up
on Halime to protect Bursa.

1088
01:44:49,000 --> 01:44:53,679
But what about Claudius? Why would
he oppose the order of the Emperor?

1089
01:44:53,760 --> 01:45:00,839
My Bey, I don't know if that dog is more
courageous than Sofia or more cowardly.

1090
01:45:00,840 --> 01:45:03,479
No, his goal is different.

1091
01:45:03,480 --> 01:45:06,519
Sofia wants to protect Bursa.

1092
01:45:06,520 --> 01:45:10,839
But Claudius wants to be the ruler of Bursa.

1093
01:45:11,200 --> 01:45:15,359
If he followed the Emperor's order, he
would only become the governor of Bursa.

1094
01:45:15,360 --> 01:45:18,359
That's why he wants to unite
with the Mongols and fight us.

1095
01:45:18,360 --> 01:45:20,719
Even if he is under their command...

1096
01:45:21,560 --> 01:45:23,879
..he will rule Bursa.

1097
01:45:23,880 --> 01:45:28,799
My Bey, do you say Claudius
and Kucar are allies now?

1098
01:45:29,320 --> 01:45:32,159
My Bey, if they are together now...

1099
01:45:32,320 --> 01:45:35,519
...it means this will be very
difficult. What will we do now?

1100
01:45:35,800 --> 01:45:36,519
No.

1101
01:45:37,320 --> 01:45:39,839
Claudius doesn't have many soldiers yet.

1102
01:45:39,840 --> 01:45:42,439
But he will surely bring Kucar to his side.

1103
01:45:42,440 --> 01:45:44,399
He will set a trap in another trap.

1104
01:45:44,400 --> 01:45:48,039
But we will attack them when
they least expect it. Hide the horses.

1105
01:45:48,720 --> 01:45:50,439
We will follow them on foot.

1106
01:45:50,440 --> 01:45:52,959
As you order my Bey. Alps!

1107
01:46:18,840 --> 01:46:21,639
The tracks are clear now.

1108
01:46:22,480 --> 01:46:24,639
There are other horse tracks too.

1109
01:46:25,360 --> 01:46:27,919
Apparently, they were not alone.

1110
01:46:39,560 --> 01:46:41,919
This is Shahzade Alaeddin's horse.

1111
01:46:42,840 --> 01:46:44,679
They are captured.

1112
01:46:48,680 --> 01:46:50,879
I should not have let him go.

1113
01:46:50,880 --> 01:46:52,959
I should not have.

1114
01:46:53,200 --> 01:46:55,959
We will find them as soon
as possible, Cerkutay Bey.

1115
01:46:56,600 --> 01:46:58,079
Which direction will we go?

1116
01:46:58,200 --> 01:47:02,159
Alaeddin's horse. It will lead us.

1117
01:47:04,080 --> 01:47:05,919
Release the horse.

1118
01:47:25,200 --> 01:47:26,559
Mother.

1119
01:47:28,440 --> 01:47:29,839
My daughter.

1120
01:47:30,440 --> 01:47:33,359
I think you should tell Alps
to guard the tribe, mother.

1121
01:47:33,360 --> 01:47:36,879
You know, someone who
betrays once may do it again.

1122
01:47:36,880 --> 01:47:38,599
She cannot be trusted.

1123
01:47:38,600 --> 01:47:40,199
Fatma.

1124
01:47:40,320 --> 01:47:41,719
Mother.

1125
01:47:42,160 --> 01:47:46,919
Do you expect me to forget all the
pain we suffered from? To ignore it?

1126
01:47:48,760 --> 01:47:51,639
Your sister didn't even want to come here.

1127
01:47:51,680 --> 01:47:57,399
Because of that snake Sofia,
your sister tried to kill herself.

1128
01:48:00,520 --> 01:48:04,239
Now you will be a big sister to
her. You won't leave her side.

1129
01:48:04,240 --> 01:48:07,399
In fact, I am giving you your first duty.

1130
01:48:07,400 --> 01:48:10,319
You will cook the herb soup together, huh?

1131
01:48:10,560 --> 01:48:13,799
Mother, I don't want to do anything with her.

1132
01:48:14,120 --> 01:48:18,439
Come on my daughter, go and take
your sister. We don't have much time.

1133
01:48:20,640 --> 01:48:22,959
Go, my daughter. Go.

1134
01:48:45,920 --> 01:48:47,879
Near Tavsantepe

1135
01:48:48,520 --> 01:48:50,439
There they are.

1136
01:49:06,160 --> 01:49:08,399
You were right, my Bey.

1137
01:49:08,400 --> 01:49:13,479
The dogs are keeping the Beys
prisoner here to lure us into a trap.

1138
01:49:18,240 --> 01:49:21,879
Claudius is not here. Let's go and kill his men.

1139
01:49:21,880 --> 01:49:23,999
Let's save the Beys.

1140
01:49:24,120 --> 01:49:25,679
We will not.

1141
01:49:25,680 --> 01:49:27,359
Why, my Bey?

1142
01:49:27,800 --> 01:49:29,719
That's why.

1143
01:49:38,520 --> 01:49:43,519
As you said, Claudius asked
for support from Kucar, my Bey.

1144
01:49:44,040 --> 01:49:46,239
And their numbers are very high.

1145
01:49:53,840 --> 01:49:59,999
Now it's clear that Claudius
left his position to meet them.

1146
01:50:01,360 --> 01:50:08,079
If we attack them with just our
swords, we cannot defeat them.

1147
01:50:10,360 --> 01:50:13,999
Boran, Turhan, you will come with me.

1148
01:50:14,000 --> 01:50:15,839
We will sneak in and take the Beys.

1149
01:50:15,840 --> 01:50:18,279
-Okay, my Bey.
-As you order, my Bey.

1150
01:50:18,280 --> 01:50:22,119
My Bey, what about me and
Abdal? What are we going to do?

1151
01:50:22,120 --> 01:50:25,239
You two will set traps on the way back.

1152
01:50:25,240 --> 01:50:28,559
We will hunt them all one
by one when they return.

1153
01:50:29,040 --> 01:50:30,919
Now listen to me carefully.

1154
01:50:53,080 --> 01:50:56,199
Did I bring you here so you
could stand there and do nothing?

1155
01:50:56,200 --> 01:50:59,399
Help me, so we can leave quickly.

1156
01:50:59,400 --> 01:51:01,359
You will choose the freshest herbs.

1157
01:51:01,360 --> 01:51:03,959
Not the ones that are too ripe. Come on.

1158
01:51:33,920 --> 01:51:36,119
I'll pick from this side.

1159
01:51:36,560 --> 01:51:40,239
Stop! Stop, there is a pit on that side.

1160
01:51:40,560 --> 01:51:42,959
You might fall.

1161
01:51:48,280 --> 01:51:53,159
You can fall. I don't care. But
I promised my Bala mother.

1162
01:51:53,160 --> 01:51:56,759
Otherwise, I wouldn't
care about a traitor like you.

1163
01:52:01,440 --> 01:52:03,959
Then don't tell me what to do.

1164
01:52:04,760 --> 01:52:08,799
Stop! Stop! Where are you going?

1165
01:52:08,800 --> 01:52:12,159
Stop! I told you to stop!

1166
01:52:13,520 --> 01:52:17,199
I said stop!

1167
01:52:17,320 --> 01:52:19,559
Stop, you will fall!

1168
01:52:20,600 --> 01:52:23,159
Stop! Stop!

1169
01:52:33,760 --> 01:52:35,719
What have you done?

1170
01:52:39,640 --> 01:52:41,039
My leg..

1171
01:52:44,160 --> 01:52:46,119
I didn't want to hurt you, but...

1172
01:52:47,280 --> 01:52:48,679
..I have to do this.

1173
01:52:53,080 --> 01:52:56,399
You are completely getting rid of me, anyway.

1174
01:53:00,320 --> 01:53:02,039
I'm leaving.

1175
01:53:04,440 --> 01:53:06,399
Stop, don"t go!

1176
01:53:06,440 --> 01:53:09,559
Stop! Don't go! Stop!

1177
01:53:10,520 --> 01:53:12,719
You people will never forgive me.

1178
01:53:13,040 --> 01:53:14,559
You will never trust me.

1179
01:53:14,880 --> 01:53:17,159
What have you done?

1180
01:53:21,200 --> 01:53:23,359
There is no place for me in this family.

1181
01:53:25,120 --> 01:53:27,959
Stop, Hali... Stop

1182
01:53:28,160 --> 01:53:29,719
I said stop!

1183
01:53:30,440 --> 01:53:33,759
You can't help betraying, huh?

1184
01:53:53,720 --> 01:53:56,319
Have they gone this way? Are you sure?

1185
01:53:56,440 --> 01:53:59,639
Yes, I saw it for myself
and informed you in no time.

1186
01:54:07,400 --> 01:54:09,239
Hush.

1187
01:54:41,200 --> 01:54:45,479
The bird is already off the
cage. It will be an easy job.

1188
01:54:46,280 --> 01:54:47,639
Let's go.

1189
01:54:59,120 --> 01:55:03,559
-Shahzade Alaaddin's dagger.
-This is Gonca Hatun's dagger.

1190
01:55:07,160 --> 01:55:08,879
Osman Bey turned out to be right.

1191
01:55:09,000 --> 01:55:11,679
Shahzade Alaaddin is in trouble.

1192
01:55:12,040 --> 01:55:15,119
We should send a message
and let him know. Come on.

1193
01:55:16,920 --> 01:55:18,959
Alps, watch out!

1194
01:55:21,560 --> 01:55:23,639
They are too many!

1195
01:55:24,200 --> 01:55:27,519
We need to fight hard. Come on, brothers.

1196
01:55:27,600 --> 01:55:28,839
Attack!

1197
01:55:36,280 --> 01:55:39,359
-Allah is Eternal!
-Allah is The Righteous!

1198
01:55:49,840 --> 01:55:51,639
Allah is the greatest!

1199
01:55:59,840 --> 01:56:01,399
Allah is the greatest!

1200
01:56:09,840 --> 01:56:11,679
Allah is the greatest!

1201
01:56:12,240 --> 01:56:13,959
Die, dastards!

1202
01:56:15,320 --> 01:56:16,599
Come here.

1203
01:56:18,240 --> 01:56:20,599
Allah is the greatest!

1204
01:56:25,280 --> 01:56:26,879
Allah is the greatest!

1205
01:56:41,080 --> 01:56:42,279
My Shahzade.

1206
01:56:42,560 --> 01:56:44,799
This is Alaaddin Bey's dagger.

1207
01:56:52,240 --> 01:56:54,519
It seems the dastards abducted him.

1208
01:56:55,400 --> 01:56:59,319
But we will find him. We will.

1209
01:57:08,040 --> 01:57:10,119
Where do you think you are going?

1210
01:57:10,440 --> 01:57:13,599
Speak now. Where is Alaaddin?

1211
01:57:14,840 --> 01:57:18,319
Where is Alaaddin? I said speak!

1212
01:57:18,760 --> 01:57:22,719
Speak and I will send you to hell with no pain.

1213
01:57:23,040 --> 01:57:23,759
Come on.

1214
01:57:23,840 --> 01:57:27,439
Kucar is going to send him to Olcaytu Khan.

1215
01:57:39,600 --> 01:57:43,439
Look at me. Where is he taking him?

1216
01:57:43,920 --> 01:57:46,639
Where is he taking him? Speak!

1217
01:57:46,920 --> 01:57:50,519
Speak! Tell me Come on!

1218
01:57:56,960 --> 01:57:59,039
As far as I know, Mongolians...

1219
01:57:59,640 --> 01:58:02,639
...make their place in the most isolated spot.

1220
01:58:03,160 --> 01:58:05,639
How will we find them?

1221
01:58:08,000 --> 01:58:09,599
We will find.

1222
01:58:10,400 --> 01:58:16,079
Even if it costs our lives, we
will find my brother Alaaddin.

1223
01:58:16,160 --> 01:58:20,079
Olcaytu will never have him.

1224
01:58:20,560 --> 01:58:22,279
Ever.

1225
01:58:25,360 --> 01:58:29,199
I will find you. Alaaddin. Hold on.

1226
01:58:30,480 --> 01:58:31,679
Hold on.

1227
02:00:11,520 --> 02:00:13,639
How can explain this to mother now?

1228
02:00:19,840 --> 02:00:21,839
How can I explain this?

1229
02:00:32,680 --> 02:00:35,079
She has a death wish, obviously.

1230
02:00:35,680 --> 02:00:37,679
How dare you come here?

1231
02:00:39,680 --> 02:00:41,439
We had to make an agreement.

1232
02:00:41,680 --> 02:00:44,039
But my patience has limits, Sofia.

1233
02:00:45,200 --> 02:00:47,039
Thanks for welcoming, Bala.

1234
02:00:49,280 --> 02:00:51,719
I'm here to stick to our agreement.

1235
02:00:52,000 --> 02:00:56,719
Claudius is laying a trap
for Osman by using Beys.

1236
02:00:57,200 --> 02:01:00,039
Explain it. What trap?

1237
02:01:00,160 --> 02:01:03,079
Claudius has called reinforcements recently.

1238
02:01:03,360 --> 02:01:04,759
His target isn't Beys.

1239
02:01:05,000 --> 02:01:08,999
He'll use them as a bait for Osman.

1240
02:01:12,000 --> 02:01:13,719
Osman..

1241
02:01:16,560 --> 02:01:20,919
Alps, sisters! Bring the horses!
We have to let Osman Bey know this!

1242
02:01:21,040 --> 02:01:25,479
I want to do what our alliance requires,
Bala. Let me join you with my soldiers.

1243
02:01:25,960 --> 02:01:28,399
We should destroy Claudius together.

1244
02:01:28,800 --> 02:01:30,919
Bala Hatun! Bala Hatun!

1245
02:01:32,360 --> 02:01:36,919
-My boy, what happened?
-Fatma Hatun is stumping.

1246
02:01:37,160 --> 02:01:40,359
What are you talking about? Fatma?

1247
02:01:41,760 --> 02:01:43,879
What happened, my dear?

1248
02:01:44,440 --> 02:01:46,599
-Mother, she's gone.
-Who?

1249
02:01:46,760 --> 02:01:49,879
-Where is Halime?
-She's gone away, mother.

1250
02:01:51,560 --> 02:01:54,839
She said she couldn't stay here. She tricked me.

1251
02:01:56,560 --> 02:01:58,439
Damn it! Poena...

1252
02:02:04,000 --> 02:02:06,399
Halime... My dear.

1253
02:02:07,320 --> 02:02:11,079
Alps, you go inform Osman
Bey quickly! I need to find Halime!

1254
02:02:11,960 --> 02:02:15,839
Sisters, take her to the healing tent.
You go ahead, my dear. Come on.

1255
02:02:21,480 --> 02:02:22,399
Bala.

1256
02:02:22,760 --> 02:02:25,839
Bala, we can find her together
more easily. I raised her!

1257
02:02:25,920 --> 02:02:29,239
Bala, nobody else can
trace her better than I can.

1258
02:02:29,280 --> 02:02:32,879
You should pray that she's
alright! This is all because of you!

1259
02:02:55,920 --> 02:02:57,479
Kucar.

1260
02:02:57,800 --> 02:03:01,359
I'm grateful that you didn't
ignore my call for help.

1261
02:03:02,200 --> 02:03:07,319
I heard that you laid the trap and
was waiting for your prey, Claudius.

1262
02:03:07,480 --> 02:03:12,159
Well... We will share the prey, of course.

1263
02:03:18,480 --> 02:03:21,679
Is this...

1264
02:03:22,120 --> 02:03:24,599
...the reinforcement that snake called?

1265
02:03:24,840 --> 02:03:26,159
Koca Bey.

1266
02:03:27,000 --> 02:03:28,959
Are they allies?

1267
02:03:39,760 --> 02:03:44,439
We drew Osman Bey into a huge trouble.

1268
02:03:46,400 --> 02:03:48,359
What a shame!

1269
02:04:02,280 --> 02:04:03,719
Osman Bey.

1270
02:04:08,000 --> 02:04:10,239
Untie Beys, come on.

1271
02:04:13,880 --> 02:04:15,519
Thank you, Boran Bey.

1272
02:04:18,640 --> 02:04:20,239
Hasan Bey.

1273
02:04:20,720 --> 02:04:22,999
Koca Bey? What happened?

1274
02:04:23,280 --> 02:04:27,639
After we sent the messenger
to you, Claudius caught us...

1275
02:04:27,920 --> 02:04:30,119
...and drew you into a trap, my Bey.

1276
02:04:33,920 --> 02:04:36,239
Whoever did this to you

1277
02:04:36,560 --> 02:04:38,799
...I won't kill them before they pay for it.

1278
02:04:38,800 --> 02:04:41,159
Don't worry. Don't worry.

1279
02:04:41,240 --> 02:04:45,759
Let's go and make them lose their minds, my Bey.

1280
02:04:46,360 --> 02:04:47,719
Well..

1281
02:04:47,840 --> 02:04:52,679
When they don't see you
here, they will lose their minds.

1282
02:04:52,720 --> 02:04:58,359
And when they come after me,
they will see what happens then.

1283
02:04:59,040 --> 02:05:02,039
You are wounded.
You can't fight like this.

1284
02:05:02,200 --> 02:05:04,519
I can't let you fight with those wounds.

1285
02:05:04,560 --> 02:05:08,519
Come on, wear the heathen clothes
and get out of the woods secretly.

1286
02:05:08,680 --> 02:05:10,599
How can we leave you, Osman Bey?

1287
02:05:10,840 --> 02:05:13,399
Just obey my orders. Come on.

1288
02:05:15,440 --> 02:05:17,039
Come on, warriors.

1289
02:05:26,200 --> 02:05:27,839
Let's go.

1290
02:05:44,640 --> 02:05:46,559
Where should I go now?

1291
02:05:56,520 --> 02:05:59,439
Where are you going Halime?

1292
02:06:01,200 --> 02:06:02,679
What do you want from me?

1293
02:06:02,680 --> 02:06:05,479
I swear you deceived everyone excellently.

1294
02:06:06,560 --> 02:06:09,119
-Stay out of my way.
-No.

1295
02:06:10,600 --> 02:06:12,839
I am here to take you.

1296
02:06:13,240 --> 02:06:16,439
Bala's most precious treasure.

1297
02:06:17,560 --> 02:06:19,999
I won't let you use me.

1298
02:06:20,640 --> 02:06:24,639
Don't worry. We will take you to your brother.

1299
02:06:25,760 --> 02:06:27,719
I am not going anywhere.

1300
02:06:28,800 --> 02:06:32,759
So you are going to tire us, huh? Take her!

1301
02:06:48,160 --> 02:06:52,079
That's Halime Hatun! Protect Halime Hatun!

1302
02:07:11,440 --> 02:07:12,639
Thank you Koca Bey.

1303
02:07:12,640 --> 02:07:14,559
Come on Hasan brother.

1304
02:07:14,680 --> 02:07:19,879
We must leave this place without
being noticed for Osman Bey's plan.

1305
02:07:24,520 --> 02:07:26,839
Come on.

1306
02:07:26,840 --> 02:07:31,599
After Alaeddin, now it's Sofia's Poena's turn.

1307
02:07:31,600 --> 02:07:34,839
Or, Osman's Halime.

1308
02:07:34,840 --> 02:07:36,319
Whatever her name is...

1309
02:07:36,320 --> 02:07:43,799
What a pity, Osman will die without hearing
the news that his daughter is taken prisoner.

1310
02:07:57,680 --> 02:07:59,639
What does this mean?

1311
02:08:01,040 --> 02:08:02,799
What happened here?

1312
02:08:04,280 --> 02:08:09,239
The cage was broken the prey ran away.

1313
02:08:09,400 --> 02:08:11,839
Is this how you take precautions, Claudius?

1314
02:08:11,840 --> 02:08:15,799
We will catch them before they reach
Osman and tell him about our trap.

1315
02:08:15,800 --> 02:08:20,279
Stop! Bring the horses!

1316
02:08:24,840 --> 02:08:26,239
Halime.

1317
02:08:27,440 --> 02:08:29,079
Halime!

1318
02:08:41,080 --> 02:08:42,159
Halime!

1319
02:08:42,160 --> 02:08:43,639
Poena!

1320
02:08:54,000 --> 02:08:55,279
Halime!

1321
02:08:55,280 --> 02:08:56,559
Poena!

1322
02:08:57,120 --> 02:08:59,079
Mother..

1323
02:09:00,600 --> 02:09:02,679
Mother!

1324
02:09:05,320 --> 02:09:06,839
Poena!

1325
02:09:07,720 --> 02:09:09,399
Sofia!

1326
02:09:10,680 --> 02:09:11,999
Begum..

1327
02:09:12,000 --> 02:09:14,439
Catch her!

1328
02:09:16,320 --> 02:09:18,919
Come, my daughter! Sofia!

1329
02:09:22,480 --> 02:09:23,999
Are you alright?

1330
02:09:32,120 --> 02:09:34,519
You shouldn't have touched my children, Begum!

1331
02:09:34,520 --> 02:09:36,039
I will never let you do that!

1332
02:09:36,040 --> 02:09:39,079
You will die just like your children, Bala.

1333
02:09:43,320 --> 02:09:44,759
Here, my daughter!

1334
02:09:57,280 --> 02:09:58,879
Attack!

1335
02:10:35,720 --> 02:10:36,799
Poena!

1336
02:10:49,400 --> 02:10:52,039
Sofia!

1337
02:10:55,640 --> 02:10:56,799
Retreat!

1338
02:10:56,800 --> 02:10:58,279
Halime!

1339
02:11:00,920 --> 02:11:02,119
Sofia!

1340
02:11:02,120 --> 02:11:04,199
Halime, are you alright, my daughter?

1341
02:11:04,200 --> 02:11:04,879
Aunt..

1342
02:11:06,520 --> 02:11:08,839
Sofia, what did you do?

1343
02:11:11,560 --> 02:11:13,519
We are even Bala.

1344
02:11:14,240 --> 02:11:18,799
Take Poena away.

1345
02:11:20,680 --> 02:11:22,639
Kismet, bring the horses.

1346
02:11:22,640 --> 02:11:25,119
We will take Sofia to the
tribe! Come on! Get up!

1347
02:11:25,120 --> 02:11:28,479
We cannot, mother!

1348
02:11:28,480 --> 02:11:30,159
What did you say?

1349
02:11:31,400 --> 02:11:33,119
You called me mother!

1350
02:11:33,120 --> 02:11:34,639
Tell me, my daughter...

1351
02:11:34,640 --> 02:11:36,559
Tell me, my daughter.

1352
02:11:36,560 --> 02:11:38,159
Alaeddin Bey...

1353
02:11:38,160 --> 02:11:39,479
My brother...

1354
02:11:41,640 --> 02:11:42,919
...was captured.

1355
02:11:43,720 --> 02:11:46,479
What?

1356
02:11:53,520 --> 02:11:55,679
Sofia. Sofia!

1357
02:11:55,680 --> 02:11:57,639
Sofia!

1358
02:12:11,840 --> 02:12:13,239
Kucar.

1359
02:12:13,240 --> 02:12:15,559
What are you doing? We need to catch them!

1360
02:12:30,240 --> 02:12:36,119
Osman Bey and the Beys are there.

1361
02:12:37,000 --> 02:12:38,599
On the contrary!

1362
02:12:51,840 --> 02:12:53,799
You are wrong!

1363
02:12:54,400 --> 02:12:56,599
I am right in front of you.

1364
02:12:57,600 --> 02:13:01,679
Osman!

1365
02:13:01,800 --> 02:13:04,599
You will call me the ruler
of the state, Osman Bey!

1366
02:13:04,600 --> 02:13:08,919
Now that there are many of
you, you are not scared, huh?

1367
02:13:09,080 --> 02:13:10,439
Remember this.

1368
02:13:10,880 --> 02:13:14,919
Countless small numbers have
overcome countless large numbers.

1369
02:13:15,760 --> 02:13:18,159
I will teach you this with my furor.